{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014HYvHmGhR6Dd6j8JZ4dfsv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C04/KK(1/10)\n4\t**CU:** C04 — Body Electrotherapy | **WA 1:** Prepare Work Area\n5\t**Paper Colour:** BLUE\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Objectives\n10\t1. Demonstrate correct PPE usage. 2. Identify, select and arrange electrotherapy equipment. 3. Perform pre-session equipment checks.\n11\t\n12\t## Equipment: All electrotherapy units, trolley, disinfectant, PPE, electrode pads, gels, towels, equipment log.\n13\t\n14\t## Procedure\n15\t1. Don PPE (apron, mask, closed-toe shoes, gloves ready). 2. Remove metallic jewellery. 3. Inspect all equipment cables for damage. 4. Check plugs and earth connections. 5. Test each machine on low setting. 6. Check electrode pads/applicators condition. 7. Record checks in equipment log. 8. Clean all equipment surfaces with disinfectant. 9. Arrange in service flow: prep zone → treatment zone → product zone → cleanup zone. 10. Ensure non-conductive surfaces, cords organised.\n16\t\n17\t## Assessment Checklist\n18\t| Criteria | C | NYC |\n19\t|----------|---|-----|\n20\t| PPE correct, jewellery removed | | |\n21\t| All equipment tested and logged | | |\n22\t| Cables inspected | | |\n23\t| Arrangement in service flow | | |\n24\t| Safety compliance | | |\n25\t\n26\t**Trainee:** _______ **Date:** _______ **Instructor:** _______\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"32bde60b-c919-4bb2-a281-28656e8c5ca6","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:19:52.089Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C04\\KK-01.md","content":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C04/KK(1/10)\n**CU:** C04 — Body Electrotherapy | **WA 1:** Prepare Work Area\n**Paper Colour:** BLUE\n\n---\n\n## Objectives\n1. Demonstrate correct PPE usage. 2. Identify, select and arrange electrotherapy equipment. 3. Perform pre-session equipment checks.\n\n## Equipment: All electrotherapy units, trolley, disinfectant, PPE, electrode pads, gels, towels, equipment log.\n\n## Procedure\n1. Don PPE (apron, mask, closed-toe shoes, gloves ready). 2. Remove metallic jewellery. 3. Inspect all equipment cables for damage. 4. Check plugs and earth connections. 5. Test each machine on low setting. 6. Check electrode pads/applicators condition. 7. Record checks in equipment log. 8. Clean all equipment surfaces with disinfectant. 9. Arrange in service flow: prep zone → treatment zone → product zone → cleanup zone. 10. Ensure non-conductive surfaces, cords organised.\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n| Criteria | C | NYC |\n|----------|---|-----|\n| PPE correct, jewellery removed | | |\n| All equipment tested and logged | | |\n| Cables inspected | | |\n| Arrangement in service flow | | |\n| Safety compliance | | |\n\n**Trainee:** _______ **Date:** _______ **Instructor:** _______\n","numLines":27,"startLine":1,"totalLines":27}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01Sz2J1Kiq2ANT6xzhNJK7i1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of all 4 KK files. Let me analyze the current state:\n\n**C01/KK-01.md** — Body Consultation / Prepare Work Area\n- Status: Well-structured with proper tables, detailed procedure steps, and a good assessment checklist\n- Missing: 5-domain checklist structure (PROCESS/OUTPUT/ATTITUDE/SAFETY/ENVIRONMENT), no AMARAN/WARNING callout, no Remarks column in checklist\n\n**C02/KK-01.md** — Body Thermal Therapy / Consultation\n\n\n- Status: Reasonably structured with tables and steps\n- Missing: 5-domain checklist structure, no AMARAN/WARNING callout, more detailed hygiene/sterilization steps\n\n**C03/KK-01.md** — Manual Body Massage / Consultation  \n- Status: VERY compact/thin — uses inline text for equipment, single-line procedure steps, minimal checklist\n- Missing: Proper structure, equipment table, safety precautions section, AMARAN/WARNING callout, expanded procedure, 5-domain checklist, client preparation steps\n\n**C04/KK-01.md** — Body Electrotherapy / Prepare Work Area\n- Status: VERY compact/thin — everything condensed into minimal formatting with objectives, equipment, and procedure all lacking proper structure and detail\n\nLooking at the patterns, I can see the standard template uses a 5-domain checklist structure covering process, output, attitude, safety, and environment, along with an AMARAN/WARNING callout and properly formatted equipment tables. The acceptance criteria require detailed client preparation, hygiene procedures, and comprehensive assessment checklists with a remarks column.\n\nMy plan is to systematically expand each file: C01 needs the AMARAN callout and more detailed hygiene steps, C03 requires a complete structural overhaul with proper tables and expanded procedures, and C04 needs the same treatment with better formatting and the full checklist framework. I'm seeing that C03 and C04 need the most work—both are minimal and require converting equipment lists to tables, adding safety sections with warnings, expanding procedures into numbered steps, and restructuring checklists into the 5-domain format. Now I need to check the NOSS extract to understand the Work Activities for each competency unit, and then look at existing C02 KK files to understand the established pattern I should follow.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1076,"cache_read_input_tokens":40143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1076},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"1bcc8777-b7df-4b40-9eb4-d1341ce2505e"}
