{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DeTVmrBuVEjqn83Zjw6ZQd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C02/KK(2/7)\n4\t**Competency Unit:** C02 — Body Thermal Therapy\n5\t**Work Activity 2:** Prepare Body Thermal Therapy Work Area\n6\t**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## Objectives (Objektif)\n11\t1. Set up the thermal therapy room/cubicle to professional standards.\n12\t2. Apply safety precautions for thermal therapy environments.\n13\t3. Test equipment functionality and confirm readiness.\n14\t4. Clean and sterilise thermal therapy equipment.\n15\t\n16\t---\n17\t\n18\t## Equipment and Materials\n19\t| Item | Qty |\n20\t|------|-----|\n21\t| Sauna/steam cabinet | 1 |\n22\t| Infrared lamp or blanket | 1 |\n23\t| Paraffin wax heater (if applicable) | 1 |\n24\t| Treatment couch | 1 |\n25\t| Trolley | 1 |\n26\t| Disinfectant spray/solution | 1 |\n27\t| Clean cloths | 4 |\n28\t| Fresh towels, bed sheets, disposable liners | As needed |\n29\t| Thermometer / temperature gauge | 1 |\n30\t| Timer | 1 |\n31\t| Equipment log book | 1 |\n32\t\n33\t---\n34\t\n35\t## Safety Precautions\n36\t1. Check all electrical cords for damage before use.\n37\t2. Ensure RCD protection is active.\n38\t3. Verify fire extinguisher (CO2) is accessible.\n39\t4. Check emergency exit door opens outward.\n40\t5. First aid kit with burn supplies accessible.\n41\t\n42\t---\n43\t\n44\t## Procedure\n45\t\n46\t### Step 1: Room Preparation\n47\t1.1 Check ventilation — exhaust fan operational.\n48\t1.2 Check floor — clean, dry, non-slip.\n49\t1.3 Set room thermostat to comfortable ambient temperature.\n50\t1.4 Ensure shower/rinse area is clean and available.\n51\t1.5 Check emergency exit; ensure door opens freely.\n52\t\n53\t### Step 2: Equipment Functionality Testing\n54\t2.1 **Sauna cabinet:** Power on; check heating element heats up; verify thermostat reads correctly; test timer; check door/latch.\n55\t2.2 **Steam cabinet:** Fill water reservoir; power on; check steam output; verify temperature gauge; test timer.\n56\t2.3 **Infrared lamp/blanket:** Power on; check heat output at low and high settings; verify timer.\n57\t2.4 **Paraffin wax heater:** Check wax level; power on; verify temperature reaches 52-54 C.\n58\t2.5 Record all test results in the equipment log book with date and signature.\n59\t\n60\t### Step 3: Clean and Sterilise Equipment\n61\t3.1 Wipe interior of sauna/steam cabinet with antibacterial solution.\n62\t3.2 Disinfect seat/bench surfaces.\n63\t3.3 Place disposable liner in cabinet seat.\n64\t3.4 Wipe infrared equipment housing with disinfectant.\n65\t3.5 Wipe treatment couch and trolley.\n66\t3.6 Place fresh linen on the treatment couch.\n67\t\n68\t### Step 4: Arrange Work Area\n69\t4.1 Arrange in service flow: consultation/preparation zone, thermal treatment zone, rinse/cool-down zone, post-treatment zone.\n70\t4.2 Place pre-treatment products on trolley.\n71\t4.3 Set out towels, drinking water, timer.\n72\t4.4 Ensure call bell / alert system for client is functional.\n73\t\n74\t### Step 5: Final Safety Check\n75\t5.1 Verify all equipment is at correct temperature.\n76\t5.2 Check water availability (drinking water, shower).\n77\t5.3 Confirm first aid kit location.\n78\t5.4 Work area ready for client.\n79\t\n80\t---\n81\t\n82\t## Assessment Checklist\n83\t\n84\t| No. | Criteria | Competent | Not Yet |\n85\t|-----|----------|-----------|---------|\n86\t| 1 | Room ventilation and flooring checked | | |\n87\t| 2 | Emergency exit verified | | |\n88\t| 3 | All thermal equipment tested and logged | | |\n89\t| 4 | Equipment cleaned and sterilised | | |\n90\t| 5 | Disposable liners placed | | |\n91\t| 6 | Work area arranged in service flow | | |\n92\t| 7 | Safety equipment accessible (fire extinguisher, first aid) | | |\n93\t| 8 | Client hydration and comfort provisions in place | | |\n94\t| 9 | Call bell functional | | |\n95\t\n96\t**Trainee:** _____________ **Date:** _____________ **Instructor:** _____________\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"910a869c-57c2-4bb5-b805-bbd7ed3807c8","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:20:09.965Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C02\\KK-02.md","content":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C02/KK(2/7)\n**Competency Unit:** C02 — Body Thermal Therapy\n**Work Activity 2:** Prepare Body Thermal Therapy Work Area\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n\n---\n\n## Objectives (Objektif)\n1. Set up the thermal therapy room/cubicle to professional standards.\n2. Apply safety precautions for thermal therapy environments.\n3. Test equipment functionality and confirm readiness.\n4. Clean and sterilise thermal therapy equipment.\n\n---\n\n## Equipment and Materials\n| Item | Qty |\n|------|-----|\n| Sauna/steam cabinet | 1 |\n| Infrared lamp or blanket | 1 |\n| Paraffin wax heater (if applicable) | 1 |\n| Treatment couch | 1 |\n| Trolley | 1 |\n| Disinfectant spray/solution | 1 |\n| Clean cloths | 4 |\n| Fresh towels, bed sheets, disposable liners | As needed |\n| Thermometer / temperature gauge | 1 |\n| Timer | 1 |\n| Equipment log book | 1 |\n\n---\n\n## Safety Precautions\n1. Check all electrical cords for damage before use.\n2. Ensure RCD protection is active.\n3. Verify fire extinguisher (CO2) is accessible.\n4. Check emergency exit door opens outward.\n5. First aid kit with burn supplies accessible.\n\n---\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Room Preparation\n1.1 Check ventilation — exhaust fan operational.\n1.2 Check floor — clean, dry, non-slip.\n1.3 Set room thermostat to comfortable ambient temperature.\n1.4 Ensure shower/rinse area is clean and available.\n1.5 Check emergency exit; ensure door opens freely.\n\n### Step 2: Equipment Functionality Testing\n2.1 **Sauna cabinet:** Power on; check heating element heats up; verify thermostat reads correctly; test timer; check door/latch.\n2.2 **Steam cabinet:** Fill water reservoir; power on; check steam output; verify temperature gauge; test timer.\n2.3 **Infrared lamp/blanket:** Power on; check heat output at low and high settings; verify timer.\n2.4 **Paraffin wax heater:** Check wax level; power on; verify temperature reaches 52-54 C.\n2.5 Record all test results in the equipment log book with date and signature.\n\n### Step 3: Clean and Sterilise Equipment\n3.1 Wipe interior of sauna/steam cabinet with antibacterial solution.\n3.2 Disinfect seat/bench surfaces.\n3.3 Place disposable liner in cabinet seat.\n3.4 Wipe infrared equipment housing with disinfectant.\n3.5 Wipe treatment couch and trolley.\n3.6 Place fresh linen on the treatment couch.\n\n### Step 4: Arrange Work Area\n4.1 Arrange in service flow: consultation/preparation zone, thermal treatment zone, rinse/cool-down zone, post-treatment zone.\n4.2 Place pre-treatment products on trolley.\n4.3 Set out towels, drinking water, timer.\n4.4 Ensure call bell / alert system for client is functional.\n\n### Step 5: Final Safety Check\n5.1 Verify all equipment is at correct temperature.\n5.2 Check water availability (drinking water, shower).\n5.3 Confirm first aid kit location.\n5.4 Work area ready for client.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n\n| No. | Criteria | Competent | Not Yet |\n|-----|----------|-----------|---------|\n| 1 | Room ventilation and flooring checked | | |\n| 2 | Emergency exit verified | | |\n| 3 | All thermal equipment tested and logged | | |\n| 4 | Equipment cleaned and sterilised | | |\n| 5 | Disposable liners placed | | |\n| 6 | Work area arranged in service flow | | |\n| 7 | Safety equipment accessible (fire extinguisher, first aid) | | |\n| 8 | Client hydration and comfort provisions in place | | |\n| 9 | Call bell functional | | |\n\n**Trainee:** _____________ **Date:** _____________ **Instructor:** _____________\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FZPKGd8iyvF2cTsZQkqKMU","type":"tool_result","content":"# NOSS Extract: Aesthetic Services Level 3\r\n\r\n**Document:** S960-002-3:2020 AESTHETIC SERVICES\r\n**Level:** 3 (Aesthetician)\r\n**Section:** (S) Other Service Activities\r\n**Group:** (960) Other Personal Service Activities\r\n**Area:** Beauty Therapy\r\n**Source PDF:** 189 pages\r\n**Date Extracted:** 2026-04-16\r\n\r\n> This file is the complete source-of-truth extraction of all competency data from the NOSS PDF.\r\n> It contains ALL work activities, knowledge, skills, attitudes, assessment criteria, training hours,\r\n> tools/equipment/materials, and competency weightage required for WIM document generation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Table of Contents\r\n\r\n1. [Document Overview](#1-document-overview)\r\n2. [Competency Profile Chart (CPC)](#2-competency-profile-chart-cpc)\r\n3. [Competency Profile (CP)](#3-competency-profile-cp)\r\n4. [CoCU 15.1 - Body Consultation](#4-cocu-151---body-consultation)\r\n5. [CoCU 15.2 - Body Thermal Therapy](#5-cocu-152---body-thermal-therapy)\r\n6. [CoCU 15.3 - Manual Body Massage](#6-cocu-153---manual-body-massage)\r\n7. [CoCU 15.4 - Body Electrotherapy](#7-cocu-154---body-electrotherapy)\r\n8. [CoCU 15.5 - Body Wrap Therapy](#8-cocu-155---body-wrap-therapy)\r\n9. [CoCU 15.6 - Salon Operational Supervision](#9-cocu-156---salon-operational-supervision)\r\n10. [CoCU 15.7 - Salon Sales and Promotional Activities](#10-cocu-157---salon-sales-and-promotional-activities)\r\n11. [CoCU 15.8 - Bust Firming Therapy (Elective)](#11-cocu-158---bust-firming-therapy-elective)\r\n12. [Delivery Mode](#12-delivery-mode)\r\n13. [Tools, Equipment and Materials (TEM)](#13-tools-equipment-and-materials-tem)\r\n14. [Competency Weightage](#14-competency-weightage)\r\n15. [Training Hours Summary](#15-training-hours-summary)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Document Overview\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Occupational Structure (OS)\r\n\r\n| Level | Title |\r\n|-------|-------|\r\n| Level 5 | Aesthetic Manager |\r\n| Level 4 | Senior Aesthetician |\r\n| Level 3 | Aesthetician |\r\n| Level 2 | Beauty Therapist |\r\n| Level 1 | Beautician |\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Occupational Area Structure (OAS)\r\n\r\n| Level | Area Title |\r\n|-------|------------|\r\n| Level 5 | Aesthetic Services Management |\r\n| Level 4 | Aesthetic Therapy Services |\r\n| Level 3 | Aesthetic Services |\r\n| Level 2 | Beauty Therapy Services |\r\n| Level 1 | Beauty Services |\r\n\r\n### 1.3 Occupational Prerequisite\r\n\r\n- Age 18 years and above\r\n- Physically fit\r\n\r\n### 1.4 Training Prerequisite\r\n\r\n- Completed Malaysian Skills Certificate (MSC) S960-002-2:2020 Beauty Therapy Services\r\n- Able to read and write in Bahasa Malaysia and/or English\r\n- Physically fit\r\n\r\n### 1.5 Competency Level 3 Definition\r\n\r\nCompetent in performing a broad range of varied work activities, performed in a variety of contexts, most of which are complex and non-routine. There is considerable responsibility and autonomy and control or guidance of others is often required.\r\n\r\n### 1.6 Occupational Competencies\r\n\r\n**Core competencies:**\r\n- (a) Body Consultation\r\n- (b) Body Thermal Therapy\r\n- (c) Manual Body Massage\r\n- (d) Body Electrotherapy\r\n- (e) Body Wrap Therapy\r\n- (f) Salon Operational Supervision\r\n- (g) Salon Sales and Promotional Activities\r\n\r\n**Elective competencies (added value):**\r\n- (h) Bust Firming Therapy\r\n\r\n### 1.7 Abbreviations\r\n\r\n| Abbr | Full Form |\r\n|------|-----------|\r\n| A&P | Anatomy and Physiology |\r\n| BMI | Body Mass Index |\r\n| DSD | Department of Skills Development |\r\n| FIFO | First-in-First-Out |\r\n| LILO | Last-in-Last-Out |\r\n| LMI | Lean Meat Index |\r\n| MSC | Malaysian Skills Certificate |\r\n| NCS | National Competency Standard |\r\n| NOSS | National Occupational Skills Standard |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"22bffc35-41fa-467c-96a7-8a6c6f95375c","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:20:14.436Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# NOSS Extract: Aesthetic Services Level 3\r\n\r\n**Document:** S960-002-3:2020 AESTHETIC SERVICES\r\n**Level:** 3 (Aesthetician)\r\n**Section:** (S) Other Service Activities\r\n**Group:** (960) Other Personal Service Activities\r\n**Area:** Beauty Therapy\r\n**Source PDF:** 189 pages\r\n**Date Extracted:** 2026-04-16\r\n\r\n> This file is the complete source-of-truth extraction of all competency data from the NOSS PDF.\r\n> It contains ALL work activities, knowledge, skills, attitudes, assessment criteria, training hours,\r\n> tools/equipment/materials, and competency weightage required for WIM document generation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Table of Contents\r\n\r\n1. [Document Overview](#1-document-overview)\r\n2. [Competency Profile Chart (CPC)](#2-competency-profile-chart-cpc)\r\n3. [Competency Profile (CP)](#3-competency-profile-cp)\r\n4. [CoCU 15.1 - Body Consultation](#4-cocu-151---body-consultation)\r\n5. [CoCU 15.2 - Body Thermal Therapy](#5-cocu-152---body-thermal-therapy)\r\n6. [CoCU 15.3 - Manual Body Massage](#6-cocu-153---manual-body-massage)\r\n7. [CoCU 15.4 - Body Electrotherapy](#7-cocu-154---body-electrotherapy)\r\n8. [CoCU 15.5 - Body Wrap Therapy](#8-cocu-155---body-wrap-therapy)\r\n9. [CoCU 15.6 - Salon Operational Supervision](#9-cocu-156---salon-operational-supervision)\r\n10. [CoCU 15.7 - Salon Sales and Promotional Activities](#10-cocu-157---salon-sales-and-promotional-activities)\r\n11. [CoCU 15.8 - Bust Firming Therapy (Elective)](#11-cocu-158---bust-firming-therapy-elective)\r\n12. [Delivery Mode](#12-delivery-mode)\r\n13. [Tools, Equipment and Materials (TEM)](#13-tools-equipment-and-materials-tem)\r\n14. [Competency Weightage](#14-competency-weightage)\r\n15. [Training Hours Summary](#15-training-hours-summary)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Document Overview\r\n\r\n### 1.1 Occupational Structure (OS)\r\n\r\n| Level | Title |\r\n|-------|-------|\r\n| Level 5 | Aesthetic Manager |\r\n| Level 4 | Senior Aesthetician |\r\n| Level 3 | Aesthetician |\r\n| Level 2 | Beauty Therapist |\r\n| Level 1 | Beautician |\r\n\r\n### 1.2 Occupational Area Structure (OAS)\r\n\r\n| Level | Area Title |\r\n|-------|------------|\r\n| Level 5 | Aesthetic Services Management |\r\n| Level 4 | Aesthetic Therapy Services |\r\n| Level 3 | Aesthetic Services |\r\n| Level 2 | Beauty Therapy Services |\r\n| Level 1 | Beauty Services |\r\n\r\n### 1.3 Occupational Prerequisite\r\n\r\n- Age 18 years and above\r\n- Physically fit\r\n\r\n### 1.4 Training Prerequisite\r\n\r\n- Completed Malaysian Skills Certificate (MSC) S960-002-2:2020 Beauty Therapy Services\r\n- Able to read and write in Bahasa Malaysia and/or English\r\n- Physically fit\r\n\r\n### 1.5 Competency Level 3 Definition\r\n\r\nCompetent in performing a broad range of varied work activities, performed in a variety of contexts, most of which are complex and non-routine. There is considerable responsibility and autonomy and control or guidance of others is often required.\r\n\r\n### 1.6 Occupational Competencies\r\n\r\n**Core competencies:**\r\n- (a) Body Consultation\r\n- (b) Body Thermal Therapy\r\n- (c) Manual Body Massage\r\n- (d) Body Electrotherapy\r\n- (e) Body Wrap Therapy\r\n- (f) Salon Operational Supervision\r\n- (g) Salon Sales and Promotional Activities\r\n\r\n**Elective competencies (added value):**\r\n- (h) Bust Firming Therapy\r\n\r\n### 1.7 Abbreviations\r\n\r\n| Abbr | Full Form |\r\n|------|-----------|\r\n| A&P | Anatomy and Physiology |\r\n| BMI | Body Mass Index |\r\n| DSD | Department of Skills Development |\r\n| FIFO | First-in-First-Out |\r\n| LILO | Last-in-Last-Out |\r\n| LMI | Lean Meat Index |\r\n| MSC | Malaysian Skills Certificate |\r\n| NCS | National Competency Standard |\r\n| NOSS | National Occupational Skills Standard |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01APpbJDD1M6EYgQdQpHhm4z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good picture. Let me look at the NOSS extract more specifically for the Work Activities of C01, C02, C03, and C04 to understand what the KK-01 files should cover.\n\nActually, let me focus on what needs to be done based on the acceptance criteria:\n1. All KK files have proper client preparation steps\n2. Hygiene and sterilization procedures are detailed\n3. Assessment checklists cover process, output, attitude, safety, environment\n\nLooking at the 4 files:\n\n**C01/KK-01** (Prepare Body Consultation Work Area) - Already well structured, but:\n\n\n- Missing: AMARAN/WARNING callout\n- Missing: 5-domain checklist (PROCESS/OUTPUT/ATTITUDE/SAFETY/ENVIRONMENT) with Remarks column\n- Client prep is covered in Step 1 (personal preparation) — good\n- Hygiene/sterilization in Step 2 (Clean and Disinfect Surfaces) — good\n\n**C02/KK-01** (Carry Out Body Thermal Therapy Consultation) - Needs work area preparation steps before the consultation, plus the warning callout and 5-domain assessment checklist with remarks. The basic structure is there but missing the hygiene preparation phase and the comprehensive evaluation framework.\n\n**C03/KK-01** (Manual Body Massage Consultation) - This one's quite sparse and needs significant expansion across equipment specifications, safety guidelines, the warning callout, detailed procedural steps, and the 5-domain checklist. Client preparation and hygiene protocols are notably absent.\n\n**C04/KK-01** (Body Electrotherapy - Prepare Work Area) - Similarly underdeveloped, requiring a full equipment table, safety precautions, warning callout, expanded procedures, and the 5-domain checklist. While there's some personal preparation mentioned, the detailed hygiene and sterilization steps need to be fleshed out.\n\nThe main additions across all four procedures are the AMARAN/WARNING callouts, the 5-domain checklists with remarks columns, and more thorough client and work area preparation details.\n\nNow I'm checking the established 5-domain pattern from the existing KK files to ensure consistency—the domains are PROCESS, OUTPUT, ATTITUDE, SAFETY, and ENVIRONMENT, each with a dedicated remarks column.\n\nLooking back at the US-005 progress notes, I realize those updates were specifically for the BEV KK procedures, not the Aesthetic ones I'm currently working on. The Aesthetic C01/KK-01 still has the old flat checklist structure, so I need to apply the same 5-domain restructuring that was done for BEV to maintain consistency across all KK files.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the specific changes needed while keeping the diff size manageable. For C01/KK-01, I'll add a warning callout in the Safety Precautions section, expand the client preparation step, include more detail on sterilization procedures, and convert the checklist to the 5-domain format with a Remarks column. For C02/KK-01, I'll follow the same pattern with the warning callout and client preparation step.\n\nC03 and C04 need more substantial work since they're missing proper structure entirely—I'll need to add headers and metadata, build out the Equipment section as a proper table, create a Safety Precautions section with the warning callout, and expand the procedures into numbered steps with clear sub-steps covering client preparation, hygiene, and the main procedure, then restructure the checklists to the 5-domain format.\n\nNow I'm calculating the diff budget—the instructions allow roughly 350 total lines of changes. Since C03 and C04 are currently very small files (36 and 27 lines), expanding each to around 80-100 lines means adding 44-64 lines per file. For C01 and C02, the changes are lighter—mainly adding the AMARAN callouts, expanding client prep details, and restructuring the checklists. I'm estimating around 20 lines of changes for C01 and 30 for C02, which should keep me well within the budget.\n\nBefore I proceed with the rewrites, I need to check what a proper 5-domain checklist structure actually looks like. I remember that US-005 was supposed to update the BEV KK files with this format, so let me look back at what was documented there to make sure I'm following the same pattern.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3636,"cache_read_input_tokens":41219,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3636},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"a945b4a8-ed8b-481d-a0fd-3e65b4ca9d3f"}
