{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qt2B3nb4gfKnh9WfPDa6rD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C02/KK(1/6)\n4\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU / BLUE\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Competency Unit: Perform Battery Management System (BMS) Rectification\n9\t## Work Activity 1: Carry Out BMS Rectification Workplace Preparation\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## Objektif Prestasi / Performance Objectives\n14\t\n15\t1. Demonstrate BMS rectification workplace preparation with HV safety protocols\n16\t2. Perform HV-specific tool and equipment inspection\n17\t3. Complete a BMS-specific JHA with HV hazard identification\n18\t4. Deploy HV isolation zone with appropriate signage and barriers\n19\t\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t## Peralatan dan Bahan / Equipment and Materials\n23\t\n24\t### Tools\n25\t| No. | Item | Quantity |\n26\t|-----|------|----------|\n27\t| 1 | Insulated tool kit (Class 0, 1000V) | 1 set |\n28\t| 2 | Common tools set | 1 set |\n29\t| 3 | Diagnostic scan tool | 1 unit |\n30\t| 4 | Digital multimeter (CAT III, 1000V) | 1 unit |\n31\t| 5 | Mega Ohm meter / insulation tester (CAT III, 1000V) | 1 unit |\n32\t\n33\t### Safety Equipment\n34\t| No. | Item | Quantity |\n35\t|-----|------|----------|\n36\t| 1 | EV Service Bay (with anti-static flooring) | 1 |\n37\t| 2 | Electric rescue hook | 1 |\n38\t| 3 | Retractable barrier stanchions | 1 set |\n39\t| 4 | Safety box | 1 |\n40\t| 5 | HV warning signage | As required |\n41\t| 6 | Insulated mat (Class 0) | 1 |\n42\t| 7 | Fire extinguisher (Class D) | 1 |\n43\t| 8 | AED (Automated External Defibrillator) | 1 (nearby) |\n44\t| 9 | Spill kit (absorbent pads, neutralising agent) | 1 |\n45\t\n46\t### PPE (Per Trainee)\n47\t| No. | Item | Specification |\n48\t|-----|------|---------------|\n49\t| 1 | Insulated gloves | Class 0 (1000V AC / 1500V DC) |\n50\t| 2 | Leather over-gloves | Per manufacturer |\n51\t| 3 | Safety glasses | MS ISO 16321 / ANSI Z87.1 |\n52\t| 4 | Dielectric safety footwear | DI rated |\n53\t| 5 | Safety helmet | MS 340 or equivalent |\n54\t\n55\t---\n56\t\n57\t## Langkah Keselamatan / Safety Precautions\n58\t\n59\t> **AMARAN / WARNING:** BMS rectification involves direct work on HV systems (200-800V DC). Fatal electrocution risk. Strict adherence to all HV safety procedures is mandatory.\n60\t\n61\t1. Full PPE mandatory at all times\n62\t2. Minimum TWO qualified persons present\n63\t3. HV work permit signed before commencing\n64\t4. Insulated gloves MUST pass air inflation test\n65\t5. Remove ALL metallic jewellery\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## Prosedur Kerja / Work Procedure\n70\t\n71\t### Step 1: HV Work Permit\n72\t1.1 Obtain HV work permit form from supervisor\n73\t1.2 Complete all sections: task description, personnel, risk assessment\n74\t1.3 Obtain supervisor signature authorising HV work\n75\t1.4 Post the permit at the work bay entry point\n76\t\n77\t### Step 2: PPE Inspection and Donning\n78\t2.1 Lay out all required PPE items on a clean surface\n79\t2.2 Perform air inflation test on insulated gloves: roll cuff towards fingers and check for air leaks; inspect for cuts, cracks, or discolouration\n80\t2.3 Inspect safety glasses for cracks, scratches, or damaged frames\n81\t2.4 Inspect dielectric footwear for damage to sole or upper\n82\t2.5 Don PPE in sequence: footwear, safety glasses, helmet, insulated gloves with leather over-gloves\n83\t\n84\t### Step 3: HV Isolation Zone Setup\n85\t3.1 Deploy retractable barrier stanchions around the entire work bay perimeter\n86\t3.2 Post HV warning signage at ALL entry points (minimum 3 signs)\n87\t3.3 Place insulated mat (Class 0) at all work positions around the vehicle\n88\t3.4 Verify HV warning signage on vehicle is visible and legible\n89\t3.5 Post \"HV WORK IN PROGRESS — AUTHORISED PERSONNEL ONLY\" notice\n90\t\n91\t### Step 4: Equipment Verification\n92\t4.1 Fire extinguisher (Class D): service date, pressure, pin\n93\t4.2 Electric rescue hook: mounted, accessible, condition verified\n94\t4.3 Safety box: positioned near work area for key and interlock storage\n95\t4.4 AED: confirm location within 30 seconds reach\n96\t4.5 Spill kit: verify contents — absorbent pads, neutralising agent, containment supplies\n97\t\n98\t### Step 5: HV Tool Inspection\n99\t5.1 Inspect insulated tools: check IEC 60900 markings, insulation integrity\n100\t5.2 Inspect digital multimeter: verify CAT III-1000V rating, leads in good condition\n101\t5.3 Inspect Mega Ohm meter: verify CAT III-1000V rating, calibration date current\n102\t5.4 Inspect lifting equipment (if battery pack work planned): capacity rating, condition\n103\t5.5 Complete tool inventory form — list all tools verified as serviceable\n104\t\n105\t### Step 6: JHA for BMS Rectification\n106\t6.1 Complete JHA with specific attention to: electrocution, arc flash, chemical exposure, crush injury, thermal runaway\n107\t6.2 Include emergency response plan for battery thermal event\n108\t6.3 Include spill containment plan\n109\t6.4 Brief all team members on JHA findings\n110\t\n111\t### Step 7: Toolbox Talk\n112\t7.1 Conduct toolbox talk with emphasis on HV-specific hazards\n113\t7.2 Review emergency procedures: electrocution response (rescue hook, call 999, CPR/AED), thermal runaway response (evacuate, Class D extinguisher, call BOMBA)\n114\t7.3 Record attendance\n115\t\n116\t---\n117\t\n118\t## Senarai Semak Penilaian / Assessment Checklist\n119\t\n120\t| No. | Assessment Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent | Remarks |\n121\t|-----|-------------------|-----------|-------------------|---------|\n122\t| **PROCESS** | | | | |\n123\t| 1 | HV work permit completed and posted at bay entry | [ ] | [ ] | |\n124\t| 2 | PPE correctly inspected — insulated gloves air test performed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n125\t| 3 | HV isolation zone established with barriers and signage | [ ] | [ ] | |\n126\t| 4 | Insulated mat placed at all work positions | [ ] | [ ] | |\n127\t| 5 | All HV tools and meters inspected and verified | [ ] | [ ] | |\n128\t| 6 | Safety equipment verified (extinguisher, rescue hook, AED, spill kit) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n129\t| 7 | JHA completed with HV-specific hazards and emergency plan | [ ] | [ ] | |\n130\t| 8 | Toolbox talk conducted covering all emergency procedures | [ ] | [ ] | |\n131\t| **OUTPUT** | | | | |\n132\t| 9 | HV isolation zone fully operational and compliant | [ ] | [ ] | |\n133\t| 10 | All documentation complete (work permit, JHA, tool inventory) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n134\t| **ATTITUDE** | | | | |\n135\t| 11 | Systematic and responsible approach to HV preparation | [ ] | [ ] | |\n136\t| 12 | Attentive to team safety and HV hazard awareness | [ ] | [ ] | |\n137\t| **SAFETY** | | | | |\n138\t| 13 | Full PPE worn correctly throughout the activity | [ ] | [ ] | |\n139\t| 14 | HV safety protocols strictly observed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n140\t| **ENVIRONMENT** | | | | |\n141\t| 15 | Workspace clean and orderly upon completion | [ ] | [ ] | |\n142\t\n143\t**Trainee Name:** _____________________ **Date:** _____________\n144\t**Instructor Name:** _____________________ **Signature:** _____________\n145\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"07c4b875-46e9-42d1-861e-5953291aa577","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:20:46.819Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C02\\KK-01.md","content":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C02/KK(1/6)\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU / BLUE\n\n---\n\n## Competency Unit: Perform Battery Management System (BMS) Rectification\n## Work Activity 1: Carry Out BMS Rectification Workplace Preparation\n\n---\n\n## Objektif Prestasi / Performance Objectives\n\n1. Demonstrate BMS rectification workplace preparation with HV safety protocols\n2. Perform HV-specific tool and equipment inspection\n3. Complete a BMS-specific JHA with HV hazard identification\n4. Deploy HV isolation zone with appropriate signage and barriers\n\n---\n\n## Peralatan dan Bahan / Equipment and Materials\n\n### Tools\n| No. | Item | Quantity |\n|-----|------|----------|\n| 1 | Insulated tool kit (Class 0, 1000V) | 1 set |\n| 2 | Common tools set | 1 set |\n| 3 | Diagnostic scan tool | 1 unit |\n| 4 | Digital multimeter (CAT III, 1000V) | 1 unit |\n| 5 | Mega Ohm meter / insulation tester (CAT III, 1000V) | 1 unit |\n\n### Safety Equipment\n| No. | Item | Quantity |\n|-----|------|----------|\n| 1 | EV Service Bay (with anti-static flooring) | 1 |\n| 2 | Electric rescue hook | 1 |\n| 3 | Retractable barrier stanchions | 1 set |\n| 4 | Safety box | 1 |\n| 5 | HV warning signage | As required |\n| 6 | Insulated mat (Class 0) | 1 |\n| 7 | Fire extinguisher (Class D) | 1 |\n| 8 | AED (Automated External Defibrillator) | 1 (nearby) |\n| 9 | Spill kit (absorbent pads, neutralising agent) | 1 |\n\n### PPE (Per Trainee)\n| No. | Item | Specification |\n|-----|------|---------------|\n| 1 | Insulated gloves | Class 0 (1000V AC / 1500V DC) |\n| 2 | Leather over-gloves | Per manufacturer |\n| 3 | Safety glasses | MS ISO 16321 / ANSI Z87.1 |\n| 4 | Dielectric safety footwear | DI rated |\n| 5 | Safety helmet | MS 340 or equivalent |\n\n---\n\n## Langkah Keselamatan / Safety Precautions\n\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** BMS rectification involves direct work on HV systems (200-800V DC). Fatal electrocution risk. Strict adherence to all HV safety procedures is mandatory.\n\n1. Full PPE mandatory at all times\n2. Minimum TWO qualified persons present\n3. HV work permit signed before commencing\n4. Insulated gloves MUST pass air inflation test\n5. Remove ALL metallic jewellery\n\n---\n\n## Prosedur Kerja / Work Procedure\n\n### Step 1: HV Work Permit\n1.1 Obtain HV work permit form from supervisor\n1.2 Complete all sections: task description, personnel, risk assessment\n1.3 Obtain supervisor signature authorising HV work\n1.4 Post the permit at the work bay entry point\n\n### Step 2: PPE Inspection and Donning\n2.1 Lay out all required PPE items on a clean surface\n2.2 Perform air inflation test on insulated gloves: roll cuff towards fingers and check for air leaks; inspect for cuts, cracks, or discolouration\n2.3 Inspect safety glasses for cracks, scratches, or damaged frames\n2.4 Inspect dielectric footwear for damage to sole or upper\n2.5 Don PPE in sequence: footwear, safety glasses, helmet, insulated gloves with leather over-gloves\n\n### Step 3: HV Isolation Zone Setup\n3.1 Deploy retractable barrier stanchions around the entire work bay perimeter\n3.2 Post HV warning signage at ALL entry points (minimum 3 signs)\n3.3 Place insulated mat (Class 0) at all work positions around the vehicle\n3.4 Verify HV warning signage on vehicle is visible and legible\n3.5 Post \"HV WORK IN PROGRESS — AUTHORISED PERSONNEL ONLY\" notice\n\n### Step 4: Equipment Verification\n4.1 Fire extinguisher (Class D): service date, pressure, pin\n4.2 Electric rescue hook: mounted, accessible, condition verified\n4.3 Safety box: positioned near work area for key and interlock storage\n4.4 AED: confirm location within 30 seconds reach\n4.5 Spill kit: verify contents — absorbent pads, neutralising agent, containment supplies\n\n### Step 5: HV Tool Inspection\n5.1 Inspect insulated tools: check IEC 60900 markings, insulation integrity\n5.2 Inspect digital multimeter: verify CAT III-1000V rating, leads in good condition\n5.3 Inspect Mega Ohm meter: verify CAT III-1000V rating, calibration date current\n5.4 Inspect lifting equipment (if battery pack work planned): capacity rating, condition\n5.5 Complete tool inventory form — list all tools verified as serviceable\n\n### Step 6: JHA for BMS Rectification\n6.1 Complete JHA with specific attention to: electrocution, arc flash, chemical exposure, crush injury, thermal runaway\n6.2 Include emergency response plan for battery thermal event\n6.3 Include spill containment plan\n6.4 Brief all team members on JHA findings\n\n### Step 7: Toolbox Talk\n7.1 Conduct toolbox talk with emphasis on HV-specific hazards\n7.2 Review emergency procedures: electrocution response (rescue hook, call 999, CPR/AED), thermal runaway response (evacuate, Class D extinguisher, call BOMBA)\n7.3 Record attendance\n\n---\n\n## Senarai Semak Penilaian / Assessment Checklist\n\n| No. | Assessment Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent | Remarks |\n|-----|-------------------|-----------|-------------------|---------|\n| **PROCESS** | | | | |\n| 1 | HV work permit completed and posted at bay entry | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 2 | PPE correctly inspected — insulated gloves air test performed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 3 | HV isolation zone established with barriers and signage | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 4 | Insulated mat placed at all work positions | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 5 | All HV tools and meters inspected and verified | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 6 | Safety equipment verified (extinguisher, rescue hook, AED, spill kit) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 7 | JHA completed with HV-specific hazards and emergency plan | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 8 | Toolbox talk conducted covering all emergency procedures | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **OUTPUT** | | | | |\n| 9 | HV isolation zone fully operational and compliant | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 10 | All documentation complete (work permit, JHA, tool inventory) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **ATTITUDE** | | | | |\n| 11 | Systematic and responsible approach to HV preparation | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 12 | Attentive to team safety and HV hazard awareness | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **SAFETY** | | | | |\n| 13 | Full PPE worn correctly throughout the activity | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 14 | HV safety protocols strictly observed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **ENVIRONMENT** | | | | |\n| 15 | Workspace clean and orderly upon completion | [ ] | [ ] | |\n\n**Trainee Name:** _____________________ **Date:** _____________\n**Instructor Name:** _____________________ **Signature:** _____________\n","numLines":145,"startLine":1,"totalLines":145}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01RQsv445r8nyAXMtbNCFr4J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have an excellent reference for the 5-domain checklist format. The BEV KK-01 file is a very well-structured example. Let me use this as a template for the aesthetic KK files.\n\nNow let me make my plan:\n\n## Current State\n- C01/KK-01: Well-structured but uses simple flat checklist (12 rows), no AMARAN/WARNING\n- C02/KK-01: Reasonably structured but flat checklist (9 rows), no AMARAN/WARNING, minimal hygiene/sterilization for consultation area\n- C03/KK-01: Very minimal (36 lines) — inline equipment text, no safety section, no AMARAN, no step structure, minimal checklist\n\n\n- C04/KK-01: Extremely minimal (27 lines) — everything compressed into one line, lacks any proper structure or AMARAN callouts\n\n## Problem Identified\nUS-012 requires:\n1. Proper client preparation steps in all KK files\n2. Detailed hygiene and sterilization procedures\n3. 5-domain assessment checklists (PROCESS/OUTPUT/ATTITUDE/SAFETY/ENVIRONMENT) with Remarks column\n\n## Planned Changes\n\n### C01/KK-01.md\n- Add AMARAN/WARNING callout in Safety Precautions\n- Rename Step 1 to be explicitly \"Client Preparation Steps\" or add note about area being ready for client\n- Add autoclave/UV sterilization detail in Step 2 (hygiene/sterilization)\n- Replace flat checklist with 5-domain checklist with Remarks column ([ ] format)\n\n### C02/KK-01.md\n- Add AMARAN/WARNING callout in Safety Precautions\n- Add Step 0 (or before Step 1): Prepare consultation area hygiene before client (disinfect surfaces, prepare fresh linen)\n- Add explicit client preparation steps (greet, seat, client comfort)\n- Replace flat checklist with 5-domain checklist with Remarks column\n\n### C03/KK-01.md\n- Full expansion from 36 to ~80-90 lines\n- Add Objectives section\n- Convert equipment to proper table\n- Add Safety Precautions with AMARAN/WARNING callout\n- Expand to numbered/sub-step procedure with: client preparation, consultation steps, hygiene/sterilization\n- Replace flat checklist with 5-domain checklist\n\n### C04/KK-01.md\n- Full expansion from 27 to ~80-90 lines\n- Add Objectives section with numbered list\n- Convert equipment to proper table\n- Add Safety Precautions section with AMARAN/WARNING callout\n- Expand procedure with client preparation, consultation steps, hygiene/sterilization procedures\n- Replace flat checklist with 5-domain checklist with Remarks column\n\nNow I'm estimating the line count changes for each document. C01 should grow by about 14 lines to reach 142 total, C02 by about 25 lines to reach 109, while C03 and C04 need full rewrites expanding from their current 36 and 27 lines respectively to around 85 lines each. That puts me at roughly 248 lines of changes, well within the 350-line budget. I'll tackle the complete rewrites for C03 and C04 first, then make targeted additions to C01 and C02.\n\nFor each consultation unit, \"client preparation\" means something slightly different depending on the context. In C01 it's about receiving and seating the client while explaining the process, in C02 it's preparing the consultation space beforehand and greeting them, C03 focuses on the consultation setting and understanding their needs, and C04 is specifically about preparing the room environment and safety measures since it's a work area setup rather than a treatment itself. For C04 especially, that means thorough sterilization and disinfection to ensure the space is safe before the client enters.\n\nNow I'm ready to start writing the implementations, beginning with C03.\n\nFor the manual body massage consultation worksheet, I need to structure it with the therapist's personal hygiene first, then prepare the consultation space with disinfection, greet and seat the client, conduct the actual consultation to gather their profile and check for contraindications, obtain their consent, and finally document everything.\n\nFor the electrotherapy work area preparation, the sequence is different since this is equipment-focused: personal preparation with PPE, safety checks on all the electrical equipment, function testing of each machine, thorough cleaning and disinfection of surfaces and electrode pads, arranging the work zones, and preparing the client environment for comfort and safety.\n\nNow I'm writing the code to generate these procedure documents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4376,"cache_read_input_tokens":44855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4376},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"ccfb6fb2-f24c-4b57-851b-1e3044c96168"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01RQsv445r8nyAXMtbNCFr4J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context I need. Here's my diagnosis and plan:\n\n## Current State\n- C01/KK-01: Well-structured (128 lines) but flat checklist, no AMARAN/WARNING\n- C02/KK-01: Reasonable (84 lines) but flat checklist, no AMARAN/WARNING, minimal hygiene for consultation prep\n- C03/KK-01: Very minimal (36 lines) — inline equipment, no safety section, no AMARAN, thin checklist\n- C04/KK-01: Very minimal (27 lines) — single-line objectives, equipment, procedure, minimal checklist\n\n## Problem Identified\nUS-012 requires: proper client preparation steps, detailed hygiene/sterilization, and 5-domain assessment checklists (PROCESS/OUTPUT/ATTITUDE/SAFETY/ENVIRONMENT with Remarks column).\n\n## Planned Changes\n- **C03/KK-01, C04/KK-01**: Full expansion — proper structure, equipment tables, safety precautions with AMARAN/WARNING, expanded procedure with client prep and hygiene steps, 5-domain checklist\n- **C01/KK-01, C02/KK-01**: Surgical additions — AMARAN/WARNING callout, client preparation detail, enhanced hygiene steps, replace flat checklist with 5-domain format\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [\n    \"aesthetic-services/C01/KK-01.md\",\n    \"aesthetic-services/C02/KK-01.md\",\n    \"aesthetic-services/C03/KK-01.md\",\n    \"aesthetic-services/C04/KK-01.md\"\n  ],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 220\n}\n</plan>\n\nStarting with C03/KK-01 (full rewrite from 36 lines to ~90):"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4376,"cache_read_input_tokens":44855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4376},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"05123720-d0bd-41af-99d1-e91295adb65e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01RQsv445r8nyAXMtbNCFr4J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NUHz1ZrCWdhpexLsASgysb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C03\\KK-01.md","content":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C03/KK(1/6)\n**Competency Unit:** C03 — Manual Body Massage / Urutan Badan Manual\n**Work Activity 1:** Carry Out Body Massage Consultation\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n\n---\n\n## Objectives (Objektif)\n\nUpon completion of this work sheet, trainees shall be able to:\n1. Prepare the consultation area to professional hygiene standards.\n2. Record client profiles for massage per PDPA requirements.\n3. Check massage-specific contraindications systematically.\n4. Obtain informed written consent before commencing treatment.\n\n---\n\n## Equipment and Materials (Peralatan dan Bahan)\n\n| Item | Quantity |\n|------|----------|\n| Consultation card / borang konsultasi | 1 |\n| Massage consent form / borang persetujuan urutan | 1 |\n| Pen, clipboard | 1 each |\n| Disinfectant spray / solution | 1 bottle |\n| Clean cloths for wiping | 2 |\n| Fresh bed sheet | 1 |\n| Fresh towels | 2 |\n| Disposable gloves | 1 pair |\n| Hand sanitiser | 1 |\n| Client gown / disposable wrap | 1 |\n\n---\n\n## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)\n\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Proceed only after completing a full contraindication check. Never carry out massage on a client with an absolute contraindication — refer to GP immediately.\n\n1. Wash hands before handling any client materials or documentation.\n2. Wear disposable gloves when handling client items or during physical assessment.\n3. Do not use shared pens without disinfecting between clients.\n4. Maintain client data confidentiality at all times (PDPA 2010).\n5. Do not proceed if an absolute contraindication is identified.\n\n---\n\n## Procedure (Prosedur)\n\n### Step 1: Personal Preparation (Persediaan Peribadi)\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap for at least 20 seconds.\n1.2 Put on clean apron and don disposable gloves.\n1.3 Check personal hygiene: clean uniform, hair tied back, no strong perfume, minimal jewellery.\n\n### Step 2: Prepare Consultation Area (Persediaan Kawasan Konsultasi)\n2.1 Spray disinfectant on the consultation couch and trolley surfaces.\n2.2 Wipe surfaces with a clean cloth in one direction; allow to air dry.\n2.3 Place a fresh bed sheet on the couch; fold towels neatly at the foot and head.\n2.4 Place disinfected consultation card, consent form, pen and clipboard on the trolley.\n2.5 Apply hand sanitiser after setup is complete.\n\n### Step 3: Client Reception and Preparation (Penerimaan dan Persediaan Klien)\n3.1 Greet the client warmly and introduce yourself.\n3.2 Escort the client to the consultation area; offer them a seat.\n3.3 Explain the purpose of the consultation and what information will be recorded.\n3.4 Provide the client gown/wrap and direct them to the changing area.\n3.5 Allow the client privacy to change; knock before re-entering.\n\n### Step 4: Record Client Profile (Rekod Profil Klien)\n4.1 Retrieve or create the client consultation card.\n4.2 Record full name, contact, date of birth, occupation.\n4.3 Ask about and record: current medical conditions, recent surgery, medications.\n4.4 Ask about: reason for massage, areas of concern, pressure preference, previous massage experience.\n4.5 Record any known allergies (including nut-based carrier oils).\n\n### Step 5: Check Contraindications (Semakan Kontraindikasi)\n5.1 Systematically check all absolute contraindications (fever, infectious skin disease, thrombosis, cancer, recent surgery, open wounds, anticoagulant medication, acute inflammation).\n5.2 Check all relative/local contraindications (varicose veins, mild hypertension, pregnancy, recent scar tissue, areas of bruising).\n5.3 Record all findings clearly on the consultation card.\n5.4 If absolute contraindication identified: inform client professionally, decline treatment, recommend GP referral.\n\n### Step 6: Obtain Informed Consent (Perolehan Persetujuan Termaklum)\n6.1 Explain the massage procedure, expected outcomes, and possible after-effects.\n6.2 Present the consent form; allow the client time to read in full.\n6.3 Answer all questions honestly.\n6.4 Obtain client signature on the consent form.\n6.5 Countersign as witness; record date.\n\n### Step 7: Documentation (Dokumentasi)\n7.1 Update the consultation card with all findings and recommendations.\n7.2 File the signed consent form with the consultation card.\n7.3 Date, sign, and initial all entries.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment Checklist (Senarai Semak Penilaian)\n\n| No. | Assessment Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent | Remarks |\n|-----|---------------------|-----------|-------------------|---------|\n| **PROCESS** | | | | |\n| 1 | Hands washed and PPE donned before setup | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 2 | Consultation area disinfected and fresh linen laid | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 3 | Client greeted, seated and prepared correctly | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 4 | Full client profile recorded on consultation card | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 5 | Contraindications checked systematically (absolute and relative) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 6 | Informed consent explained and signed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 7 | Documentation dated, signed and filed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **OUTPUT** | | | | |\n| 8 | Consultation card complete with all required fields | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 9 | Signed consent form filed with client record | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **ATTITUDE** | | | | |\n| 10 | Professional, empathetic communication maintained | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 11 | Client privacy and confidentiality respected (PDPA) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **SAFETY** | | | | |\n| 12 | Absolute contraindication identified and handled correctly | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 13 | Personal hygiene and PPE standards observed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **ENVIRONMENT** | | | | |\n| 14 | Consultation area hygienic and orderly throughout | [ ] | [ ] | |\n\n**Trainee Name:** ______________________ **Date:** ______________\n**Instructor Name:** ______________________ **Signature:** ______________\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4376,"cache_read_input_tokens":44855,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4376},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"71b2cd9a-5d6d-4417-8b89-7137deb17428"}
