 or during physical assessment.\n3. Do not use shared pens without disinfecting between clients.\n4. Maintain client data confidentiality at all times (PDPA 2010).\n5. Do not proceed if an absolute contraindication is identified.\n\n---\n\n## Procedure (Prosedur)\n\n### Step 1: Personal Preparation (Persediaan Peribadi)\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap for at least 20 seconds.\n1.2 Put on clean apron and don disposable gloves.\n1.3 Check personal hygiene: clean uniform, hair tied back, no strong perfume, minimal jewellery.\n\n### Step 2: Prepare Consultation Area (Persediaan Kawasan Konsultasi)\n2.1 Spray disinfectant on the consultation couch and trolley surfaces.\n2.2 Wipe surfaces with a clean cloth in one direction; allow to air dry.\n2.3 Place a fresh bed sheet on the couch; fold towels neatly at the foot and head.\n2.4 Place disinfected consultation card, consent form, pen and clipboard on the trolley.\n2.5 Apply hand sanitiser after setup is complete.\n\n### Step 3: Client Reception and Preparation (Penerimaan dan Persediaan Klien)\n3.1 Greet the client warmly and introduce yourself.\n3.2 Escort the client to the consultation area; offer them a seat.\n3.3 Explain the purpose of the consultation and what information will be recorded.\n3.4 Provide the client gown/wrap and direct them to the changing area.\n3.5 Allow the client privacy to change; knock before re-entering.\n\n### Step 4: Record Client Profile (Rekod Profil Klien)\n4.1 Retrieve or create the client consultation card.\n4.2 Record full name, contact, date of birth, occupation.\n4.3 Ask about and record: current medical conditions, recent surgery, medications.\n4.4 Ask about: reason for massage, areas of concern, pressure preference, previous massage experience.\n4.5 Record any known allergies (including nut-based carrier oils).\n\n### Step 5: Check Contraindications (Semakan Kontraindikasi)\n5.1 Systematically check all absolute contraindications (fever, infectious skin disease, thrombosis, cancer, recent surgery, open wounds, anticoagulant medication, acute inflammation).\n5.2 Check all relative/local contraindications (varicose veins, mild hypertension, pregnancy, recent scar tissue, areas of bruising).\n5.3 Record all findings clearly on the consultation card.\n5.4 If absolute contraindication identified: inform client professionally, decline treatment, recommend GP referral.\n\n### Step 6: Obtain Informed Consent (Perolehan Persetujuan Termaklum)\n6.1 Explain the massage procedure, expected outcomes, and possible after-effects.\n6.2 Present the consent form; allow the client time to read in full.\n6.3 Answer all questions honestly.\n6.4 Obtain client signature on the consent form.\n6.5 Countersign as witness; record date.\n\n### Step 7: Documentation (Dokumentasi)\n7.1 Update the consultation card with all findings and recommendations.\n7.2 File the signed consent form with the consultation card.\n7.3 Date, sign, and initial all entries.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment Checklist (Senarai Semak Penilaian)\n\n| No. | Assessment Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent | Remarks |\n|-----|---------------------|-----------|-------------------|---------|\n| **PROCESS** | | | | |\n| 1 | Hands washed and PPE donned before setup | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 2 | Consultation area disinfected and fresh linen laid | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 3 | Client greeted, seated and prepared correctly | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 4 | Full client profile recorded on consultation card | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 5 | Contraindications checked systematically (absolute and relative) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 6 | Informed consent explained and signed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 7 | Documentation dated, signed and filed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **OUTPUT** | | | | |\n| 8 | Consultation card complete with all required fields | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 9 | Signed consent form filed with client record | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **ATTITUDE** | | | | |\n| 10 | Professional, empathetic communication maintained | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 11 | Client privacy and confidentiality respected (PDPA) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **SAFETY** | | | | |\n| 12 | Absolute contraindication identified and handled correctly | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 13 | Personal hygiene and PPE standards observed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **ENVIRONMENT** | | | | |\n| 14 | Consultation area hygienic and orderly throughout | [ ] | [ ] | |\n\n**Trainee Name:** ______________________ **Date:** ______________\n**Instructor Name:** ______________________ **Signature:** ______________\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":35,"newStart":1,"newLines":122,"lines":[" # KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET"," "," **Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C03/KK(1/6)","-**CU:** C03 — Manual Body Massage | **WA 1:** Consultation","-**Paper Colour:** BLUE","+**Competency Unit:** C03 — Manual Body Massage / Urutan Badan Manual","+**Work Activity 1:** Carry Out Body Massage Consultation","+**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU"," "," ---"," ","-## Objectives","-1. Record client profiles for massage per PDPA.","-2. Check massage-specific contraindications.","-3. Determine client requirements and obtain consent.","+## Objectives (Objektif)"," ","-## Equipment: Consultation card, consent form, pen, clipboard.","+Upon completion of this work sheet, trainees shall be able to:","+1. Prepare the consultation area to professional hygiene standards.","+2. Record client profiles for massage per PDPA requirements.","+3. Check massage-specific contraindications systematically.","+4. Obtain informed written consent before commencing treatment."," ","-## Procedure","-1. Retrieve/create client consultation card.","-2. Review medical history, allergies.","-3. Ask about: reason for massage, areas of concern, pressure preference, previous experience.","-4. Check absolute and relative contraindications systematically.","-5. Record all massage-specific findings.","-6. Explain procedure, expected benefits and possible after-effects.","-7. Obtain written informed consent.","-8. Date and sign.","+---"," ","-## Assessment Checklist","-| Criteria | C | NYC |","-|----------|---|-----|","-| Profile recorded per PDPA | | |","-| Contraindications checked | | |","-| Massage-specific data collected | | |","-| Informed consent obtained | | |","-| Professional communication | | |","+## Equipment and Materials (Peralatan dan Bahan)"," ","-**Trainee:** _____________ **Date:** _____________ **Instructor:** _____________","+| Item | Quantity |","+|------|----------|","+| Consultation card / borang konsultasi | 1 |","+| Massage consent form / borang persetujuan urutan | 1 |","+| Pen, clipboard | 1 each |","+| Disinfectant spray / solution | 1 bottle |","+| Clean cloths for wiping | 2 |","+| Fresh bed sheet | 1 |","+| Fresh towels | 2 |","+| Disposable gloves | 1 pair |","+| Hand sanitiser | 1 |","+| Client gown / disposable wrap | 1 |","+","+---","+","+## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)","+","+> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Proceed only after completing a full contraindication check. Never carry out massage on a client with an absolute contraindication — refer to GP immediately.","+","+1. Wash hands before handling any client materials or documentation.","+2. Wear disposable gloves when handling client items or during physical assessment.","+3. Do not use shared pens without disinfecting between clients.","+4. Maintain client data confidentiality at all times (PDPA 2010).","+5. Do not proceed if an absolute contraindication is identified.","+","+---","+","+## Procedure (Prosedur)","+","+### Step 1: Personal Preparation (Persediaan Peribadi)","+1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap for at least 20 seconds.","+1.2 Put on clean apron and don disposable gloves.","+1.3 Check personal hygiene: clean uniform, hair tied back, no strong perfume, minimal jewellery.","+","+### Step 2: Prepare Consultation Area (Persediaan Kawasan Konsultasi)","+2.1 Spray disinfectant on the consultation couch and trolley surfaces.","+2.2 Wipe surfaces with a clean cloth in one direction; allow to air dry.","+2.3 Place a fresh bed sheet on the couch; fold towels neatly at the foot and head.","+2.4 Place disinfected consultation card, consent form, pen and clipboard on the trolley.","+2.5 Apply hand sanitiser after setup is complete.","+","+### Step 3: Client Reception and Preparation (Penerimaan dan Persediaan Klien)","+3.1 Greet the client warmly and introduce yourself.","+3.2 Escort the client to the consultation area; offer them a seat.","+3.3 Explain the purpose of the consultation and what information will be recorded.","+3.4 Provide the client gown/wrap and direct them to the changing area.","+3.5 Allow the client privacy to change; knock before re-entering.","+","+### Step 4: Record Client Profile (Rekod Profil Klien)","+4.1 Retrieve or create the client consultation card.","+4.2 Record full name, contact, date of birth, occupation.","+4.3 Ask about and record: current medical conditions, recent surgery, medications.","+4.4 Ask about: reason for massage, areas of concern, pressure preference, previous massage experience.","+4.5 Record any known allergies (including nut-based carrier oils).","+","+### Step 5: Check Contraindications (Semakan Kontraindikasi)","+5.1 Systematically check all absolute contraindications (fever, infectious skin disease, thrombosis, cancer, recent surgery, open wounds, anticoagulant medication, acute inflammation).","+5.2 Check all relative/local contraindications (varicose veins, mild hypertension, pregnancy, recent scar tissue, areas of bruising).","+5.3 Record all findings clearly on the consultation card.","+5.4 If absolute contraindication identified: inform client professionally, decline treatment, recommend GP referral.","+","+### Step 6: Obtain Informed Consent (Perolehan Persetujuan Termaklum)","+6.1 Explain the massage procedure, expected outcomes, and possible after-effects.","+6.2 Present the consent form; allow the client time to read in full.","+6.3 Answer all questions honestly.","+6.4 Obtain client signature on the consent form.","+6.5 Countersign as witness; record date.","+","+### Step 7: Documentation (Dokumentasi)","+7.1 Update the consultation card with all findings and recommendations.","+7.2 File the signed consent form with the consultation card.","+7.3 Date, sign, and initial all entries.","+","+---","+","+## Assessment Checklist (Senarai Semak Penilaian)","+","+| No. | Assessment Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent | Remarks |","+|-----|---------------------|-----------|-------------------|---------|","+| **PROCESS** | | | | |","+| 1 | Hands washed and PPE donned before setup | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 2 | Consultation area disinfected and fresh linen laid | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 3 | Client greeted, seated and prepared correctly | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 4 | Full client profile recorded on consultation card | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 5 | Contraindications checked systematically (absolute and relative) | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 6 | Informed consent explained and signed | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 7 | Documentation dated, signed and filed | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| **OUTPUT** | | | | |","+| 8 | Consultation card complete with all required fields | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 9 | Signed consent form filed with client record | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| **ATTITUDE** | | | | |","+| 10 | Professional, empathetic communication maintained | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 11 | Client privacy and confidentiality respected (PDPA) | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| **SAFETY** | | | | |","+| 12 | Absolute contraindication identified and handled correctly | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| 13 | Personal hygiene and PPE standards observed | [ ] | [ ] | |","+| **ENVIRONMENT** | | | | |","+| 14 | Consultation area hygienic and orderly throughout | [ ] | [ ] | |","+","+**Trainee Name:** ______________________ **Date:** ______________","+**Instructor Name:** ______________________ **Signature:** ______________"]}],"originalFile":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C03/KK(1/6)\n**CU:** C03 — Manual Body Massage | **WA 1:** Consultation\n**Paper Colour:** BLUE\n\n---\n\n## Objectives\n1. Record client profiles for massage per PDPA.\n2. Check massage-specific contraindications.\n3. Determine client requirements and obtain consent.\n\n## Equipment: Consultation card, consent form, pen, clipboard.\n\n## Procedure\n1. Retrieve/create client consultation card.\n2. Review medical history, allergies.\n3. Ask about: reason for massage, areas of concern, pressure preference, previous experience.\n4. Check absolute and relative contraindications systematically.\n5. Record all massage-specific findings.\n6. Explain procedure, expected benefits and possible after-effects.\n7. Obtain written informed consent.\n8. Date and sign.\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n| Criteria | C | NYC |\n|----------|---|-----|\n| Profile recorded per PDPA | | |\n| Contraindications checked | | |\n| Massage-specific data collected | | |\n| Informed consent obtained | | |\n| Professional communication | | |\n\n**Trainee:** _____________ **Date:** _____________ **Instructor:** _____________\n"}}
