{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_0181XPBdiWp76DnvanR4Xqdm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gocr3QbsWhS8qKPe9BdWRo","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C01\\KK-01.md","old_string":"## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)\n\n1. Wear appropriate PPE (apron) during cleaning and setup.\n2. Ensure no wet floors or tripping hazards.\n3. Check electrical equipment cords for damage before plugging in.\n4. Do not overload electrical sockets.\n5. Ensure fire extinguisher and first aid kit are accessible.","new_string":"## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)\n\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Use only approved disinfectant solutions at correct dilution. Never mix different chemical disinfectants — toxic fumes can result. Wear gloves when handling cleaning chemicals.\n\n1. Wear appropriate PPE (apron, disposable gloves) during cleaning and setup.\n2. Ensure no wet floors or tripping hazards.\n3. Check electrical equipment cords for damage before plugging in.\n4. Do not overload electrical sockets.\n5. Ensure fire extinguisher and first aid kit are accessible."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2305,"cache_read_input_tokens":53034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2305},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"3e4c4598-1ffb-4fc1-8d39-65b8456e598c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gocr3QbsWhS8qKPe9BdWRo","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C01\\KK-01.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"3f58b5f1-e436-4946-9c76-8f77706127c7","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:22:29.849Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C01\\KK-01.md","oldString":"## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)\n\n1. Wear appropriate PPE (apron) during cleaning and setup.\n2. Ensure no wet floors or tripping hazards.\n3. Check electrical equipment cords for damage before plugging in.\n4. Do not overload electrical sockets.\n5. Ensure fire extinguisher and first aid kit are accessible.","newString":"## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)\n\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Use only approved disinfectant solutions at correct dilution. Never mix different chemical disinfectants — toxic fumes can result. Wear gloves when handling cleaning chemicals.\n\n1. Wear appropriate PPE (apron, disposable gloves) during cleaning and setup.\n2. Ensure no wet floors or tripping hazards.\n3. Check electrical equipment cords for damage before plugging in.\n4. Do not overload electrical sockets.\n5. Ensure fire extinguisher and first aid kit are accessible.","originalFile":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C01/KK(1/5)\n**Competency Unit:** C01 — Body Consultation / Konsultasi Badan\n**Work Activity 1:** Prepare Body Consultation Work Area\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n\n---\n\n## Objectives (Objektif)\n\nUpon completion of this work sheet, trainees shall be able to:\n1. Demonstrate proper hygiene and safety practices for a body consultation service area.\n2. Identify, select and arrange tools, equipment and materials for body consultation.\n3. Set up a complete body consultation work station ready for client service.\n\n---\n\n## Equipment and Materials (Peralatan dan Bahan)\n\n| Item | Quantity |\n|------|----------|\n| Consultation couch/bed | 1 |\n| Trolley | 1 |\n| Therapist stool | 1 |\n| Privacy screen/curtain | 1 |\n| Measuring tape | 1 |\n| Weighing scale (digital) | 1 |\n| Stadiometer / height rod | 1 |\n| Body fat calliper | 1 |\n| Magnifying lamp | 1 |\n| BMI chart / calculator | 1 |\n| Disinfectant spray/solution | 1 bottle |\n| Clean cloths for wiping | 3 |\n| Fresh bed sheet | 1 |\n| Fresh towels (large) | 2 |\n| Fresh towels (small/hand) | 2 |\n| Consultation cards/forms (blank) | 5 |\n| Pens | 2 |\n| Clipboard | 1 |\n| Disposable gloves | 2 pairs |\n| Client gown / disposable wrap | 1 |\n| Slippers | 1 pair |\n| Tissue box | 1 |\n| Hand sanitiser | 1 |\n\n---\n\n## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)\n\n1. Wear appropriate PPE (apron) during cleaning and setup.\n2. Ensure no wet floors or tripping hazards.\n3. Check electrical equipment cords for damage before plugging in.\n4. Do not overload electrical sockets.\n5. Ensure fire extinguisher and first aid kit are accessible.\n\n---\n\n## Procedure (Prosedur)\n\n### Step 1: Personal Preparation\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.\n1.2 Put on clean apron.\n1.3 Ensure personal hygiene standards are met (clean uniform, hair tied, minimal jewellery).\n\n### Step 2: Clean and Disinfect Surfaces\n2.1 Spray disinfectant on the consultation couch surface.\n2.2 Wipe thoroughly with a clean cloth in one direction.\n2.3 Repeat for trolley top, stool, and any counter surfaces.\n2.4 Allow surfaces to air dry or wipe with a dry cloth.\n\n### Step 3: Lay Fresh Linen\n3.1 Place a fresh bed sheet on the consultation couch, tucking corners securely.\n3.2 Place one large towel folded at the foot of the couch.\n3.3 Place one large towel folded at the head of the couch (for client draping).\n3.4 Place small/hand towels on the trolley.\n\n### Step 4: Arrange Tools on Trolley\n4.1 Top shelf: Measuring tape, body fat calliper, BMI chart/calculator, pen, clipboard.\n4.2 Middle shelf: Disposable gloves, tissues, hand sanitiser, consultation cards.\n4.3 Bottom shelf: Client gown/wrap, slippers, spare towels.\n4.4 Ensure items are arranged in order of use for efficient workflow.\n\n### Step 5: Set Up Equipment\n5.1 Position the weighing scale on a flat, hard surface near the couch.\n5.2 Calibrate the digital scale to zero.\n5.3 Position the stadiometer near the weighing scale.\n5.4 Position the magnifying lamp near the head of the couch; check bulb is working.\n5.5 Plug in and test all electrical equipment.\n\n### Step 6: Set Privacy\n6.1 Position the privacy screen or ensure the curtain is properly hung.\n6.2 Check that the change area is enclosed and provides adequate privacy.\n6.3 Place hooks for client clothing in the change area.\n\n### Step 7: Prepare Documentation\n7.1 Place 5 blank consultation cards/forms on the clipboard or desk.\n7.2 Ensure pens are working.\n7.3 Have the client record file/folder accessible.\n\n### Step 8: Final Check\n8.1 Stand back and survey the entire work area.\n8.2 Check room temperature (24-26 C) and adjust if needed.\n8.3 Ensure adequate lighting.\n8.4 Confirm all items are in place and the area is presentable.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment Checklist (Senarai Semak Penilaian)\n\n| No. | Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent |\n|-----|----------|-----------|-------------------|\n| 1 | Personal hygiene and PPE observed | | |\n| 2 | All surfaces disinfected correctly | | |\n| 3 | Fresh linen properly laid on couch | | |\n| 4 | Tools arranged on trolley in order of use | | |\n| 5 | Weighing scale calibrated to zero | | |\n| 6 | Stadiometer positioned correctly | | |\n| 7 | Magnifying lamp tested and working | | |\n| 8 | Privacy screen/curtain properly set | | |\n| 9 | Documentation prepared and accessible | | |\n| 10 | Room temperature and lighting appropriate | | |\n| 11 | Safety: No tripping hazards, electrical safety observed | | |\n| 12 | Overall work area neat and professional | | |\n\n**Trainee Name:** ______________________ **Date:** ______________\n**Instructor Name:** ______________________ **Signature:** ______________\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":48,"oldLines":7,"newStart":48,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," ## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)"," ","-1. Wear appropriate PPE (apron) during cleaning and setup.","+> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Use only approved disinfectant solutions at correct dilution. Never mix different chemical disinfectants — toxic fumes can result. Wear gloves when handling cleaning chemicals.","+","+1. Wear appropriate PPE (apron, disposable gloves) during cleaning and setup."," 2. Ensure no wet floors or tripping hazards."," 3. Check electrical equipment cords for damage before plugging in."," 4. Do not overload electrical sockets."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JDBJtmFhhdZ1UsEHkgYSgj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BHkKtKJgEreQn2GK9DmoqX","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C01\\KK-01.md","old_string":"### Step 1: Personal Preparation\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.\n1.2 Put on clean apron.\n1.3 Ensure personal hygiene standards are met (clean uniform, hair tied, minimal jewellery).\n\n### Step 2: Clean and Disinfect Surfaces\n2.1 Spray disinfectant on the consultation couch surface.\n2.2 Wipe thoroughly with a clean cloth in one direction.\n2.3 Repeat for trolley top, stool, and any counter surfaces.\n2.4 Allow surfaces to air dry or wipe with a dry cloth.","new_string":"### Step 1: Personal Preparation and Client Readiness (Persediaan Peribadi dan Persediaan Klien)\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap for at least 20 seconds.\n1.2 Put on clean apron and don disposable gloves.\n1.3 Ensure personal hygiene standards are met (clean uniform, hair tied, minimal jewellery).\n1.4 Prepare client gown/wrap, slippers and towels so they are ready before the client arrives.\n\n### Step 2: Clean, Disinfect and Sterilise (Pembersihan, Penyahkuman dan Pensterilan)\n2.1 Spray approved disinfectant solution on the consultation couch surface.\n2.2 Wipe thoroughly with a clean cloth in one direction; discard used cloth.\n2.3 Repeat for trolley top, stool, and all counter surfaces.\n2.4 Wipe measuring instruments (calliper, measuring tape) with 70% isopropyl alcohol.\n2.5 Allow all surfaces and instruments to air dry completely before placing items on them."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":469,"cache_read_input_tokens":55339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":469},"output_tokens":66,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"a5575f15-afd6-40fe-b4fe-602825e291f6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BHkKtKJgEreQn2GK9DmoqX","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C01\\KK-01.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"18416ba9-0d87-4c35-8fc9-26fea8d20fbe","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:22:39.245Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C01\\KK-01.md","oldString":"### Step 1: Personal Preparation\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.\n1.2 Put on clean apron.\n1.3 Ensure personal hygiene standards are met (clean uniform, hair tied, minimal jewellery).\n\n### Step 2: Clean and Disinfect Surfaces\n2.1 Spray disinfectant on the consultation couch surface.\n2.2 Wipe thoroughly with a clean cloth in one direction.\n2.3 Repeat for trolley top, stool, and any counter surfaces.\n2.4 Allow surfaces to air dry or wipe with a dry cloth.","newString":"### Step 1: Personal Preparation and Client Readiness (Persediaan Peribadi dan Persediaan Klien)\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap for at least 20 seconds.\n1.2 Put on clean apron and don disposable gloves.\n1.3 Ensure personal hygiene standards are met (clean uniform, hair tied, minimal jewellery).\n1.4 Prepare client gown/wrap, slippers and towels so they are ready before the client arrives.\n\n### Step 2: Clean, Disinfect and Sterilise (Pembersihan, Penyahkuman dan Pensterilan)\n2.1 Spray approved disinfectant solution on the consultation couch surface.\n2.2 Wipe thoroughly with a clean cloth in one direction; discard used cloth.\n2.3 Repeat for trolley top, stool, and all counter surfaces.\n2.4 Wipe measuring instruments (calliper, measuring tape) with 70% isopropyl alcohol.\n2.5 Allow all surfaces and instruments to air dry completely before placing items on them.","originalFile":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C01/KK(1/5)\n**Competency Unit:** C01 — Body Consultation / Konsultasi Badan\n**Work Activity 1:** Prepare Body Consultation Work Area\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n\n---\n\n## Objectives (Objektif)\n\nUpon completion of this work sheet, trainees shall be able to:\n1. Demonstrate proper hygiene and safety practices for a body consultation service area.\n2. Identify, select and arrange tools, equipment and materials for body consultation.\n3. Set up a complete body consultation work station ready for client service.\n\n---\n\n## Equipment and Materials (Peralatan dan Bahan)\n\n| Item | Quantity |\n|------|----------|\n| Consultation couch/bed | 1 |\n| Trolley | 1 |\n| Therapist stool | 1 |\n| Privacy screen/curtain | 1 |\n| Measuring tape | 1 |\n| Weighing scale (digital) | 1 |\n| Stadiometer / height rod | 1 |\n| Body fat calliper | 1 |\n| Magnifying lamp | 1 |\n| BMI chart / calculator | 1 |\n| Disinfectant spray/solution | 1 bottle |\n| Clean cloths for wiping | 3 |\n| Fresh bed sheet | 1 |\n| Fresh towels (large) | 2 |\n| Fresh towels (small/hand) | 2 |\n| Consultation cards/forms (blank) | 5 |\n| Pens | 2 |\n| Clipboard | 1 |\n| Disposable gloves | 2 pairs |\n| Client gown / disposable wrap | 1 |\n| Slippers | 1 pair |\n| Tissue box | 1 |\n| Hand sanitiser | 1 |\n\n---\n\n## Safety Precautions (Langkah Keselamatan)\n\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Use only approved disinfectant solutions at correct dilution. Never mix different chemical disinfectants — toxic fumes can result. Wear gloves when handling cleaning chemicals.\n\n1. Wear appropriate PPE (apron, disposable gloves) during cleaning and setup.\n2. Ensure no wet floors or tripping hazards.\n3. Check electrical equipment cords for damage before plugging in.\n4. Do not overload electrical sockets.\n5. Ensure fire extinguisher and first aid kit are accessible.\n\n---\n\n## Procedure (Prosedur)\n\n### Step 1: Personal Preparation\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.\n1.2 Put on clean apron.\n1.3 Ensure personal hygiene standards are met (clean uniform, hair tied, minimal jewellery).\n\n### Step 2: Clean and Disinfect Surfaces\n2.1 Spray disinfectant on the consultation couch surface.\n2.2 Wipe thoroughly with a clean cloth in one direction.\n2.3 Repeat for trolley top, stool, and any counter surfaces.\n2.4 Allow surfaces to air dry or wipe with a dry cloth.\n\n### Step 3: Lay Fresh Linen\n3.1 Place a fresh bed sheet on the consultation couch, tucking corners securely.\n3.2 Place one large towel folded at the foot of the couch.\n3.3 Place one large towel folded at the head of the couch (for client draping).\n3.4 Place small/hand towels on the trolley.\n\n### Step 4: Arrange Tools on Trolley\n4.1 Top shelf: Measuring tape, body fat calliper, BMI chart/calculator, pen, clipboard.\n4.2 Middle shelf: Disposable gloves, tissues, hand sanitiser, consultation cards.\n4.3 Bottom shelf: Client gown/wrap, slippers, spare towels.\n4.4 Ensure items are arranged in order of use for efficient workflow.\n\n### Step 5: Set Up Equipment\n5.1 Position the weighing scale on a flat, hard surface near the couch.\n5.2 Calibrate the digital scale to zero.\n5.3 Position the stadiometer near the weighing scale.\n5.4 Position the magnifying lamp near the head of the couch; check bulb is working.\n5.5 Plug in and test all electrical equipment.\n\n### Step 6: Set Privacy\n6.1 Position the privacy screen or ensure the curtain is properly hung.\n6.2 Check that the change area is enclosed and provides adequate privacy.\n6.3 Place hooks for client clothing in the change area.\n\n### Step 7: Prepare Documentation\n7.1 Place 5 blank consultation cards/forms on the clipboard or desk.\n7.2 Ensure pens are working.\n7.3 Have the client record file/folder accessible.\n\n### Step 8: Final Check\n8.1 Stand back and survey the entire work area.\n8.2 Check room temperature (24-26 C) and adjust if needed.\n8.3 Ensure adequate lighting.\n8.4 Confirm all items are in place and the area is presentable.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment Checklist (Senarai Semak Penilaian)\n\n| No. | Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent |\n|-----|----------|-----------|-------------------|\n| 1 | Personal hygiene and PPE observed | | |\n| 2 | All surfaces disinfected correctly | | |\n| 3 | Fresh linen properly laid on couch | | |\n| 4 | Tools arranged on trolley in order of use | | |\n| 5 | Weighing scale calibrated to zero | | |\n| 6 | Stadiometer positioned correctly | | |\n| 7 | Magnifying lamp tested and working | | |\n| 8 | Privacy screen/curtain properly set | | |\n| 9 | Documentation prepared and accessible | | |\n| 10 | Room temperature and lighting appropriate | | |\n| 11 | Safety: No tripping hazards, electrical safety observed | | |\n| 12 | Overall work area neat and professional | | |\n\n**Trainee Name:** ______________________ **Date:** ______________\n**Instructor Name:** ______________________ **Signature:** ______________\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":60,"oldLines":16,"newStart":60,"newLines":18,"lines":[" "," ## Procedure (Prosedur)"," ","-### Step 1: Personal Preparation","-1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.","-1.2 Put on clean apron.","+### Step 1: Personal Preparation and Client Readiness (Persediaan Peribadi dan Persediaan Klien)","+1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap for at least 20 seconds.","+1.2 Put on clean apron and don disposable gloves."," 1.3 Ensure personal hygiene standards are met (clean uniform, hair tied, minimal jewellery).","+1.4 Prepare client gown/wrap, slippers and towels so they are ready before the client arrives."," ","-### Step 2: Clean and Disinfect Surfaces","-2.1 Spray disinfectant on the consultation couch surface.","-2.2 Wipe thoroughly with a clean cloth in one direction.","-2.3 Repeat for trolley top, stool, and any counter surfaces.","-2.4 Allow surfaces to air dry or wipe with a dry cloth.","+### Step 2: Clean, Disinfect and Sterilise (Pembersihan, Penyahkuman dan Pensterilan)","+2.1 Spray approved disinfectant solution on the consultation couch surface.","+2.2 Wipe thoroughly with a clean cloth in one direction; discard used cloth.","+2.3 Repeat for trolley top, stool, and all counter surfaces.","+2.4 Wipe measuring instruments (calliper, measuring tape) with 70% isopropyl alcohol.","+2.5 Allow all surfaces and instruments to air dry completely before placing items on them."," "," ### Step 3: Lay Fresh Linen"," 3.1 Place a fresh bed sheet on the consultation couch, tucking corners securely."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
