{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01GpGfp6wzfv7EjPkh6pPQMG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LwqUh7yk4uzmSWbGFU8FY1","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C02\\KK-01.md","old_string":"## Safety Precautions\n1. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.\n2. Maintain client data confidentiality.","new_string":"## Safety Precautions\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Never proceed with thermal therapy consultation without completing a full contraindication check. Thermal treatments carry serious cardiovascular and circulatory risks. Refer all absolute contraindications to a GP before any treatment.\n\n1. Wash hands and disinfect consultation surfaces before each client.\n2. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.\n3. Maintain client data confidentiality (PDPA 2010).\n4. Keep blood pressure monitor calibrated and in service."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":56415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":915},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"abf9f510-c67d-4c52-a902-4228f4060322"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LwqUh7yk4uzmSWbGFU8FY1","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C02\\KK-01.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"a3376eef-4427-43c3-833a-153799567a4c","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:22:56.521Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C02\\KK-01.md","oldString":"## Safety Precautions\n1. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.\n2. Maintain client data confidentiality.","newString":"## Safety Precautions\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Never proceed with thermal therapy consultation without completing a full contraindication check. Thermal treatments carry serious cardiovascular and circulatory risks. Refer all absolute contraindications to a GP before any treatment.\n\n1. Wash hands and disinfect consultation surfaces before each client.\n2. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.\n3. Maintain client data confidentiality (PDPA 2010).\n4. Keep blood pressure monitor calibrated and in service.","originalFile":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C02/KK(1/7)\n**Competency Unit:** C02 — Body Thermal Therapy\n**Work Activity 1:** Carry Out Body Thermal Therapy Consultation\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n\n---\n\n## Objectives (Objektif)\n1. Record client personal profiles for thermal therapy per Data Protection Act.\n2. Check client contraindications specific to thermal therapy.\n3. Determine client thermal therapy service requirements.\n4. Obtain informed consent.\n\n---\n\n## Equipment and Materials\n| Item | Qty |\n|------|-----|\n| Consultation card/form | 1 |\n| Thermal therapy consent form | 1 |\n| Blood pressure monitor (if available) | 1 |\n| Pen, clipboard | 1 each |\n\n---\n\n## Safety Precautions\n1. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.\n2. Maintain client data confidentiality.\n\n---\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Obtain and Review Client Profile\n1.1 Retrieve client's body consultation card (from C01).\n1.2 Review existing medical history, allergies, and conditions.\n1.3 Record additional thermal-specific data: heat tolerance, circulatory conditions, blood pressure, heat-affecting medications, previous thermal therapy experience.\n\n### Step 2: Check Contraindications\n2.1 Systematically check absolute contraindications (cardiovascular disease, thrombosis, severe hypertension, fever, skin infections, uncontrolled epilepsy, cancer, recent surgery, open wounds).\n2.2 Check relative contraindications (pregnancy, diabetes, mild hypertension, varicose veins, metal implants, asthma, claustrophobia).\n2.3 Record all findings.\n2.4 If absolute contraindication found: inform client, decline treatment, recommend GP.\n\n### Step 3: Determine Service Requirements\n3.1 Discuss client's primary goal (detoxification, weight loss, relaxation, cellulite reduction).\n3.2 Consider body condition from C01 consultation.\n3.3 Match client needs with available thermal therapy methods.\n3.4 Recommend appropriate thermal therapy type, frequency and duration.\n3.5 Discuss cost and treatment course.\n\n### Step 4: Obtain Informed Consent\n4.1 Explain the selected thermal therapy procedure to the client.\n4.2 Explain expected benefits and potential risks.\n4.3 Present the consent form; allow client time to read.\n4.4 Answer all client questions.\n4.5 Obtain client signature on the consent form.\n4.6 Countersign as witness.\n\n### Step 5: Record and Update\n5.1 Update consultation card with all thermal therapy consultation findings.\n5.2 File consent form with consultation card.\n5.3 Date and sign entry.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n\n| No. | Criteria | Competent | Not Yet |\n|-----|----------|-----------|---------|\n| 1 | Client profile reviewed and updated | | |\n| 2 | Thermal-specific data recorded | | |\n| 3 | Contraindications checked systematically | | |\n| 4 | Service requirements determined with client | | |\n| 5 | Thermal method recommended appropriately | | |\n| 6 | Consent form explained thoroughly | | |\n| 7 | Informed consent obtained with signatures | | |\n| 8 | Records updated and filed | | |\n| 9 | Professional communication throughout | | |\n\n**Trainee:** _____________ **Date:** _____________ **Instructor:** _____________\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":9,"newStart":26,"newLines":13,"lines":[" ---"," "," ## Safety Precautions","-1. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.","-2. Maintain client data confidentiality.","+> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Never proceed with thermal therapy consultation without completing a full contraindication check. Thermal treatments carry serious cardiovascular and circulatory risks. Refer all absolute contraindications to a GP before any treatment."," ","+1. Wash hands and disinfect consultation surfaces before each client.","+2. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.","+3. Maintain client data confidentiality (PDPA 2010).","+4. Keep blood pressure monitor calibrated and in service.","+"," ---"," "," ## Procedure"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01JLovtzqTMLZeKDhwYt59cX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018A8eGvuQg7aDaFFvukZchH","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C02\\KK-01.md","old_string":"## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Obtain and Review Client Profile","new_string":"## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Prepare Consultation Area and Receive Client (Persediaan Kawasan dan Penerimaan Klien)\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.\n1.2 Spray disinfectant on the consultation desk, chair, and any surfaces the client will contact; wipe dry.\n1.3 Place a fresh consultation card and consent form on a clean clipboard.\n1.4 Greet the client warmly; offer a seat in the consultation area.\n1.5 Explain that a brief health consultation will be conducted before any treatment.\n\n### Step 2: Obtain and Review Client Profile"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":57330,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380},"output_tokens":72,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"c9a7f93b-6395-45df-8303-326fdb3d1f0b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018A8eGvuQg7aDaFFvukZchH","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C02\\KK-01.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"bed1bb3d-7a25-4933-b28e-d06fe62ccacf","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:23:02.631Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C02\\KK-01.md","oldString":"## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Obtain and Review Client Profile","newString":"## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Prepare Consultation Area and Receive Client (Persediaan Kawasan dan Penerimaan Klien)\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.\n1.2 Spray disinfectant on the consultation desk, chair, and any surfaces the client will contact; wipe dry.\n1.3 Place a fresh consultation card and consent form on a clean clipboard.\n1.4 Greet the client warmly; offer a seat in the consultation area.\n1.5 Explain that a brief health consultation will be conducted before any treatment.\n\n### Step 2: Obtain and Review Client Profile","originalFile":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C02/KK(1/7)\n**Competency Unit:** C02 — Body Thermal Therapy\n**Work Activity 1:** Carry Out Body Thermal Therapy Consultation\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n\n---\n\n## Objectives (Objektif)\n1. Record client personal profiles for thermal therapy per Data Protection Act.\n2. Check client contraindications specific to thermal therapy.\n3. Determine client thermal therapy service requirements.\n4. Obtain informed consent.\n\n---\n\n## Equipment and Materials\n| Item | Qty |\n|------|-----|\n| Consultation card/form | 1 |\n| Thermal therapy consent form | 1 |\n| Blood pressure monitor (if available) | 1 |\n| Pen, clipboard | 1 each |\n\n---\n\n## Safety Precautions\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Never proceed with thermal therapy consultation without completing a full contraindication check. Thermal treatments carry serious cardiovascular and circulatory risks. Refer all absolute contraindications to a GP before any treatment.\n\n1. Wash hands and disinfect consultation surfaces before each client.\n2. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.\n3. Maintain client data confidentiality (PDPA 2010).\n4. Keep blood pressure monitor calibrated and in service.\n\n---\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Obtain and Review Client Profile\n1.1 Retrieve client's body consultation card (from C01).\n1.2 Review existing medical history, allergies, and conditions.\n1.3 Record additional thermal-specific data: heat tolerance, circulatory conditions, blood pressure, heat-affecting medications, previous thermal therapy experience.\n\n### Step 2: Check Contraindications\n2.1 Systematically check absolute contraindications (cardiovascular disease, thrombosis, severe hypertension, fever, skin infections, uncontrolled epilepsy, cancer, recent surgery, open wounds).\n2.2 Check relative contraindications (pregnancy, diabetes, mild hypertension, varicose veins, metal implants, asthma, claustrophobia).\n2.3 Record all findings.\n2.4 If absolute contraindication found: inform client, decline treatment, recommend GP.\n\n### Step 3: Determine Service Requirements\n3.1 Discuss client's primary goal (detoxification, weight loss, relaxation, cellulite reduction).\n3.2 Consider body condition from C01 consultation.\n3.3 Match client needs with available thermal therapy methods.\n3.4 Recommend appropriate thermal therapy type, frequency and duration.\n3.5 Discuss cost and treatment course.\n\n### Step 4: Obtain Informed Consent\n4.1 Explain the selected thermal therapy procedure to the client.\n4.2 Explain expected benefits and potential risks.\n4.3 Present the consent form; allow client time to read.\n4.4 Answer all client questions.\n4.5 Obtain client signature on the consent form.\n4.6 Countersign as witness.\n\n### Step 5: Record and Update\n5.1 Update consultation card with all thermal therapy consultation findings.\n5.2 File consent form with consultation card.\n5.3 Date and sign entry.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment Checklist\n\n| No. | Criteria | Competent | Not Yet |\n|-----|----------|-----------|---------|\n| 1 | Client profile reviewed and updated | | |\n| 2 | Thermal-specific data recorded | | |\n| 3 | Contraindications checked systematically | | |\n| 4 | Service requirements determined with client | | |\n| 5 | Thermal method recommended appropriately | | |\n| 6 | Consent form explained thoroughly | | |\n| 7 | Informed consent obtained with signatures | | |\n| 8 | Records updated and filed | | |\n| 9 | Professional communication throughout | | |\n\n**Trainee:** _____________ **Date:** _____________ **Instructor:** _____________\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":37,"oldLines":7,"newStart":37,"newLines":14,"lines":[" "," ## Procedure"," ","-### Step 1: Obtain and Review Client Profile","+### Step 1: Prepare Consultation Area and Receive Client (Persediaan Kawasan dan Penerimaan Klien)","+1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.","+1.2 Spray disinfectant on the consultation desk, chair, and any surfaces the client will contact; wipe dry.","+1.3 Place a fresh consultation card and consent form on a clean clipboard.","+1.4 Greet the client warmly; offer a seat in the consultation area.","+1.5 Explain that a brief health consultation will be conducted before any treatment.","+","+### Step 2: Obtain and Review Client Profile"," 1.1 Retrieve client's body consultation card (from C01)."," 1.2 Review existing medical history, allergies, and conditions."," 1.3 Record additional thermal-specific data: heat tolerance, circulatory conditions, blood pressure, heat-affecting medications, previous thermal therapy experience."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
