{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HxDLW5EgiG3AxmGZeS4XeE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n2\t\n3\t**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C02/KK(1/7)\n4\t**Competency Unit:** C02 — Body Thermal Therapy\n5\t**Work Activity 1:** Carry Out Body Thermal Therapy Consultation\n6\t**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## Objectives (Objektif)\n11\t1. Record client personal profiles for thermal therapy per Data Protection Act.\n12\t2. Check client contraindications specific to thermal therapy.\n13\t3. Determine client thermal therapy service requirements.\n14\t4. Obtain informed consent.\n15\t\n16\t---\n17\t\n18\t## Equipment and Materials\n19\t| Item | Qty |\n20\t|------|-----|\n21\t| Consultation card/form | 1 |\n22\t| Thermal therapy consent form | 1 |\n23\t| Blood pressure monitor (if available) | 1 |\n24\t| Pen, clipboard | 1 each |\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## Safety Precautions\n29\t> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Never proceed with thermal therapy consultation without completing a full contraindication check. Thermal treatments carry serious cardiovascular and circulatory risks. Refer all absolute contraindications to a GP before any treatment.\n30\t\n31\t1. Wash hands and disinfect consultation surfaces before each client.\n32\t2. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.\n33\t3. Maintain client data confidentiality (PDPA 2010).\n34\t4. Keep blood pressure monitor calibrated and in service.\n35\t\n36\t---\n37\t\n38\t## Procedure\n39\t\n40\t### Step 1: Prepare Consultation Area and Receive Client (Persediaan Kawasan dan Penerimaan Klien)\n41\t1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.\n42\t1.2 Spray disinfectant on the consultation desk, chair, and any surfaces the client will contact; wipe dry.\n43\t1.3 Place a fresh consultation card and consent form on a clean clipboard.\n44\t1.4 Greet the client warmly; offer a seat in the consultation area.\n45\t1.5 Explain that a brief health consultation will be conducted before any treatment.\n46\t\n47\t### Step 2: Obtain and Review Client Profile (Rekod dan Semak Profil Klien)\n48\t2.1 Retrieve client's body consultation card (from C01).\n49\t2.2 Review existing medical history, allergies, and conditions.\n50\t2.3 Record additional thermal-specific data: heat tolerance, circulatory conditions, blood pressure, heat-affecting medications, previous thermal therapy experience.\n51\t\n52\t### Step 3: Check Contraindications (Semakan Kontraindikasi)\n53\t3.1 Systematically check absolute contraindications (cardiovascular disease, thrombosis, severe hypertension, fever, skin infections, uncontrolled epilepsy, cancer, recent surgery, open wounds).\n54\t3.2 Check relative contraindications (pregnancy, diabetes, mild hypertension, varicose veins, metal implants, asthma, claustrophobia).\n55\t3.3 Record all findings.\n56\t3.4 If absolute contraindication found: inform client, decline treatment, recommend GP.\n57\t\n58\t### Step 4: Determine Service Requirements (Tentukan Keperluan Perkhidmatan)\n59\t4.1 Discuss client's primary goal (detoxification, weight loss, relaxation, cellulite reduction).\n60\t4.2 Consider body condition from C01 consultation.\n61\t4.3 Match client needs with available thermal therapy methods.\n62\t4.4 Recommend appropriate thermal therapy type, frequency and duration.\n63\t4.5 Discuss cost and treatment course.\n64\t\n65\t### Step 5: Obtain Informed Consent (Perolehan Persetujuan Termaklum)\n66\t5.1 Explain the selected thermal therapy procedure to the client.\n67\t5.2 Explain expected benefits and potential risks.\n68\t5.3 Present the consent form; allow client time to read.\n69\t5.4 Answer all client questions.\n70\t5.5 Obtain client signature on the consent form.\n71\t5.6 Countersign as witness.\n72\t\n73\t### Step 6: Record and Update (Rekod dan Kemaskini)\n74\t6.1 Update consultation card with all thermal therapy consultation findings.\n75\t6.2 File consent form with consultation card.\n76\t6.3 Date and sign entry.\n77\t\n78\t---\n79\t\n80\t## Assessment Checklist (Senarai Semak Penilaian)\n81\t\n82\t| No. | Assessment Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent | Remarks |\n83\t|-----|---------------------|-----------|-------------------|---------|\n84\t| **PROCESS** | | | | |\n85\t| 1 | Hands washed and consultation surfaces disinfected before client | [ ] | [ ] | |\n86\t| 2 | Client greeted and seated; purpose of consultation explained | [ ] | [ ] | |\n87\t| 3 | Client profile retrieved and thermal-specific data recorded | [ ] | [ ] | |\n88\t| 4 | Contraindications checked systematically (absolute and relative) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n89\t| 5 | Service requirements determined with client | [ ] | [ ] | |\n90\t| 6 | Thermal method recommended appropriately based on client needs | [ ] | [ ] | |\n91\t| 7 | Informed consent explained thoroughly and obtained with signatures | [ ] | [ ] | |\n92\t| 8 | Records updated, dated, signed and filed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n93\t| **OUTPUT** | | | | |\n94\t| 9 | Consultation card complete with all thermal-specific findings | [ ] | [ ] | |\n95\t| 10 | Signed consent form filed with client record | [ ] | [ ] | |\n96\t| **ATTITUDE** | | | | |\n97\t| 11 | Professional and empathetic communication maintained throughout | [ ] | [ ] | |\n98\t| 12 | Client privacy and data confidentiality observed (PDPA 2010) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n99\t| **SAFETY** | | | | |\n100\t| 13 | Absolute contraindication correctly identified and handled | [ ] | [ ] | |\n101\t| **ENVIRONMENT** | | | | |\n102\t| 14 | Consultation area hygienic and disinfected between clients | [ ] | [ ] | |\n103\t\n104\t**Trainee:** _____________ **Date:** _____________ **Instructor:** _____________\n105\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"efa3c3c5-bbb5-4426-9888-00e01809b546","uuid":"9fb0d7b7-860f-4a6c-9874-168c6cb200cd","timestamp":"2026-04-16T14:23:35.436Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C02\\KK-01.md","content":"# KERTAS KERJA / WORK SHEET\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C02/KK(1/7)\n**Competency Unit:** C02 — Body Thermal Therapy\n**Work Activity 1:** Carry Out Body Thermal Therapy Consultation\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** BLUE / BIRU\n\n---\n\n## Objectives (Objektif)\n1. Record client personal profiles for thermal therapy per Data Protection Act.\n2. Check client contraindications specific to thermal therapy.\n3. Determine client thermal therapy service requirements.\n4. Obtain informed consent.\n\n---\n\n## Equipment and Materials\n| Item | Qty |\n|------|-----|\n| Consultation card/form | 1 |\n| Thermal therapy consent form | 1 |\n| Blood pressure monitor (if available) | 1 |\n| Pen, clipboard | 1 each |\n\n---\n\n## Safety Precautions\n> **AMARAN / WARNING:** Never proceed with thermal therapy consultation without completing a full contraindication check. Thermal treatments carry serious cardiovascular and circulatory risks. Refer all absolute contraindications to a GP before any treatment.\n\n1. Wash hands and disinfect consultation surfaces before each client.\n2. Do not proceed if absolute contraindication is identified.\n3. Maintain client data confidentiality (PDPA 2010).\n4. Keep blood pressure monitor calibrated and in service.\n\n---\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Prepare Consultation Area and Receive Client (Persediaan Kawasan dan Penerimaan Klien)\n1.1 Wash hands thoroughly with antibacterial soap.\n1.2 Spray disinfectant on the consultation desk, chair, and any surfaces the client will contact; wipe dry.\n1.3 Place a fresh consultation card and consent form on a clean clipboard.\n1.4 Greet the client warmly; offer a seat in the consultation area.\n1.5 Explain that a brief health consultation will be conducted before any treatment.\n\n### Step 2: Obtain and Review Client Profile (Rekod dan Semak Profil Klien)\n2.1 Retrieve client's body consultation card (from C01).\n2.2 Review existing medical history, allergies, and conditions.\n2.3 Record additional thermal-specific data: heat tolerance, circulatory conditions, blood pressure, heat-affecting medications, previous thermal therapy experience.\n\n### Step 3: Check Contraindications (Semakan Kontraindikasi)\n3.1 Systematically check absolute contraindications (cardiovascular disease, thrombosis, severe hypertension, fever, skin infections, uncontrolled epilepsy, cancer, recent surgery, open wounds).\n3.2 Check relative contraindications (pregnancy, diabetes, mild hypertension, varicose veins, metal implants, asthma, claustrophobia).\n3.3 Record all findings.\n3.4 If absolute contraindication found: inform client, decline treatment, recommend GP.\n\n### Step 4: Determine Service Requirements (Tentukan Keperluan Perkhidmatan)\n4.1 Discuss client's primary goal (detoxification, weight loss, relaxation, cellulite reduction).\n4.2 Consider body condition from C01 consultation.\n4.3 Match client needs with available thermal therapy methods.\n4.4 Recommend appropriate thermal therapy type, frequency and duration.\n4.5 Discuss cost and treatment course.\n\n### Step 5: Obtain Informed Consent (Perolehan Persetujuan Termaklum)\n5.1 Explain the selected thermal therapy procedure to the client.\n5.2 Explain expected benefits and potential risks.\n5.3 Present the consent form; allow client time to read.\n5.4 Answer all client questions.\n5.5 Obtain client signature on the consent form.\n5.6 Countersign as witness.\n\n### Step 6: Record and Update (Rekod dan Kemaskini)\n6.1 Update consultation card with all thermal therapy consultation findings.\n6.2 File consent form with consultation card.\n6.3 Date and sign entry.\n\n---\n\n## Assessment Checklist (Senarai Semak Penilaian)\n\n| No. | Assessment Criteria | Competent | Not Yet Competent | Remarks |\n|-----|---------------------|-----------|-------------------|---------|\n| **PROCESS** | | | | |\n| 1 | Hands washed and consultation surfaces disinfected before client | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 2 | Client greeted and seated; purpose of consultation explained | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 3 | Client profile retrieved and thermal-specific data recorded | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 4 | Contraindications checked systematically (absolute and relative) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 5 | Service requirements determined with client | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 6 | Thermal method recommended appropriately based on client needs | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 7 | Informed consent explained thoroughly and obtained with signatures | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 8 | Records updated, dated, signed and filed | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **OUTPUT** | | | | |\n| 9 | Consultation card complete with all thermal-specific findings | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 10 | Signed consent form filed with client record | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **ATTITUDE** | | | | |\n| 11 | Professional and empathetic communication maintained throughout | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| 12 | Client privacy and data confidentiality observed (PDPA 2010) | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **SAFETY** | | | | |\n| 13 | Absolute contraindication correctly identified and handled | [ ] | [ ] | |\n| **ENVIRONMENT** | | | | |\n| 14 | Consultation area hygienic and disinfected between clients | [ ] | [ ] | |\n\n**Trainee:** _____________ **Date:** _____________ **Instructor:** _____________\n","numLines":105,"startLine":1,"totalLines":105}}}
